1
00:00:00,470 --> 00:02:02,360
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

2
00:02:03,890 --> 00:02:08,300
No living creature was harmed
during the filming of this series.

3
00:02:09,770 --> 00:02:14,200
Episode 102

4
00:02:17,640 --> 00:02:19,690
I will cut off your head, Osman.

5
00:02:19,690 --> 00:02:21,780
You can't even cut my beard.

6
00:02:42,860 --> 00:02:44,940
Come with me

7
00:02:50,040 --> 00:02:51,830
You tried to kill me, right?

8
00:02:52,390 --> 00:02:54,330
There is no going back for this anymore.

9
00:02:54,400 --> 00:02:55,840
You will die, Öktem.

10
00:02:55,870 --> 00:02:58,050
If I were to do my job with the arrow...

11
00:02:58,110 --> 00:03:00,130
I will not draw the sword, you infidel!

12
00:03:00,190 --> 00:03:01,390
Beys!

13
00:03:05,160 --> 00:03:07,770
If your intention is to seek justice...

14
00:03:07,860 --> 00:03:09,730
I say you have to wait for Osman Bey.

15
00:03:09,770 --> 00:03:11,550
Don't test my patience, Öktem Bey.

16
00:03:11,600 --> 00:03:12,890
Why don't you listen?

17
00:03:13,300 --> 00:03:14,950
Stop.

18
00:03:19,490 --> 00:03:21,560
If someone overstepped his bounds...

19
00:03:22,220 --> 00:03:23,840
he is.

20
00:03:24,820 --> 00:03:27,310
My blood has been shed
on this land, Turgut Bey.

21
00:03:28,030 --> 00:03:29,370
I won't ignore it.

22
00:03:29,620 --> 00:03:32,240
- Soldiers!
- Alps!

23
00:03:40,300 --> 00:03:42,810
I say we will resolve this
matter calmly, Öktem Bey.

24
00:03:42,930 --> 00:03:44,370
But you don't listen to me!

25
00:03:44,410 --> 00:03:45,730
You pull the sword.

26
00:03:45,770 --> 00:03:47,040
You shoot arrows.

27
00:03:48,150 --> 00:03:50,300
I won't compromise with you anymore.

28
00:03:50,630 --> 00:03:51,790
You will be arrested.

29
00:03:57,020 --> 00:03:58,090
Turgut Bey.

30
00:03:58,510 --> 00:04:00,620
Please, do something.

31
00:04:00,930 --> 00:04:02,430
Where is Osman Bey?

32
00:04:05,320 --> 00:04:07,480
Do what you want to do, Turgut Bey?

33
00:04:08,460 --> 00:04:10,240
The talk is over.

34
00:04:10,580 --> 00:04:12,030
Don't do it, Öktem Bey.

35
00:04:13,490 --> 00:04:14,650
Don't.

36
00:04:20,350 --> 00:04:21,820
You are bleeding, Osman.

37
00:04:22,500 --> 00:04:24,010
I will make all your blood flow.

38
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:30,000
Come and see.

39
00:04:36,110 --> 00:04:37,790
You can't defeat me Osman.

40
00:04:37,790 --> 00:04:39,290
Let's see.

41
00:04:57,300 --> 00:04:59,510
Another one to get revenge for.

42
00:04:59,550 --> 00:05:02,170
When you have no more blood to bleed...

43
00:05:03,060 --> 00:05:05,470
there will be no revenge you take.

44
00:05:37,860 --> 00:05:39,840
Emperor Andronikos...

45
00:05:40,750 --> 00:05:42,690
invites you to meet him.

46
00:05:45,250 --> 00:05:47,150
If someone doesn't want to stop...

47
00:05:48,170 --> 00:05:50,470
I'll have to go with his body.

48
00:05:57,440 --> 00:05:58,960
Why are you standing, Beys?

49
00:05:59,110 --> 00:06:00,780
Draw your swords.

50
00:06:03,110 --> 00:06:07,360
When you get into trouble, you come
to the tribe of Öktem Bey.

51
00:06:07,440 --> 00:06:09,280
Why this hesitation now?

52
00:06:11,760 --> 00:06:13,300
Don't, beys.

53
00:06:14,430 --> 00:06:15,900
Who draws his sword now...

54
00:06:16,110 --> 00:06:18,390
he pulls his sword on Osman Bey.

55
00:06:19,600 --> 00:06:21,600
Your eyes are blind to see the truth.

56
00:06:21,640 --> 00:06:24,350
I won't let you drag the Beys
into that darkness.

57
00:06:24,390 --> 00:06:26,290
How dare you, Alçiçek Hatun?

58
00:06:30,810 --> 00:06:31,910
Öktem Bey.

59
00:06:33,110 --> 00:06:37,150
If you don't trust justice and draw
the sword before it's time...

60
00:06:37,630 --> 00:06:38,990
you become a rebel.

61
00:06:40,130 --> 00:06:43,460
And you know that killing the rebel is
our duty. Don't do this.

62
00:06:53,680 --> 00:06:55,240
Be careful, Alps.

63
00:07:19,620 --> 00:07:20,840
Turgut Bey.

64
00:07:21,630 --> 00:07:23,250
Alps have surrounded the tribe.

65
00:07:23,310 --> 00:07:25,870
They're waiting for your command.

66
00:07:35,180 --> 00:07:36,660
There is no going back for this.

67
00:07:40,390 --> 00:07:42,370
Trust in the justice of Osman Bey.

68
00:07:42,760 --> 00:07:44,450
Tell your Alps...

69
00:07:44,970 --> 00:07:47,500
to put down their swords, Öktem Bey.

70
00:07:47,500 --> 00:07:50,100
What justice are you
talking about, Turgut Bey?

71
00:07:50,480 --> 00:07:52,180
Does Osman have justice?

72
00:07:53,860 --> 00:07:55,900
This ignoble that you brought
into our tribe....

73
00:07:55,900 --> 00:07:58,130
his hands are stained with
the blood of our heroes.

74
00:07:58,140 --> 00:07:59,790
Both were stained with my brother's blood.

75
00:07:59,790 --> 00:08:01,620
Osman Bey's balance is off.

76
00:08:01,640 --> 00:08:04,230
We will not leave my father
a victim of his justice.

77
00:08:04,280 --> 00:08:06,410
We don't trust
to the words of the infidels.

78
00:08:07,090 --> 00:08:08,840
We stand behind Öktem Bey.

79
00:08:09,190 --> 00:08:12,110
We stand behind you with the Alps.

80
00:08:12,550 --> 00:08:14,840
What you are saying is not
acceptable, Uraz Bey.

81
00:08:14,870 --> 00:08:17,370
Do you want to make
the brothers kill each other?

82
00:08:17,390 --> 00:08:20,790
They are all of us, and they are
all of our blood.

83
00:08:26,690 --> 00:08:27,940
Öktem Bey.

84
00:08:31,140 --> 00:08:35,120
Give up before it gets any worse.

85
00:08:37,700 --> 00:08:38,890
Come on.

86
00:08:54,380 --> 00:08:55,380
You...

87
00:08:56,420 --> 00:08:58,460
Who are you protecting, Commander?

88
00:08:58,480 --> 00:09:01,090
I only protect Rome, Commander Olof.

89
00:09:01,130 --> 00:09:04,000
Ophelia wanted to kill the emperor.

90
00:09:04,400 --> 00:09:07,130
Osman was the reason for her escape.

91
00:09:07,690 --> 00:09:09,130
Commander Remus!

92
00:09:10,810 --> 00:09:12,320
If you protect him...

93
00:09:12,850 --> 00:09:15,280
I will kill you and kill him.

94
00:09:20,070 --> 00:09:21,120
Osman Bey...

95
00:09:21,770 --> 00:09:25,150
Welcome back to save Rome.

96
00:09:25,970 --> 00:09:27,720
I give you my respect.

97
00:09:28,940 --> 00:09:30,570
The emperor is waiting for you.

98
00:09:31,160 --> 00:09:32,860
Thank you.

99
00:09:33,610 --> 00:09:34,930
Then...

100
00:09:36,720 --> 00:09:38,610
Let's go see the emperor.

101
00:09:38,610 --> 00:09:40,060
The Emperor

102
00:09:40,420 --> 00:09:42,350
Is he in a state to
give orders?

103
00:09:42,710 --> 00:09:44,840
What are you up to?

104
00:09:44,860 --> 00:09:46,490
Sarkis ran away.

105
00:09:46,510 --> 00:09:47,870
Ophelia ran away.

106
00:09:47,940 --> 00:09:50,390
It is not you who will do justice.

107
00:09:52,250 --> 00:09:53,560
Know your limits.

108
00:09:54,270 --> 00:10:00,010
You speak too confidently as
someone who protects traitors.

109
00:10:00,060 --> 00:10:03,620
You are too brave for someone whose axe
is useless.

110
00:10:03,810 --> 00:10:06,770
If you don't break your
courage, your head will break.

111
00:10:09,830 --> 00:10:12,350
Let's not make the emperor
wait any longer.

112
00:10:15,150 --> 00:10:16,240
Let's go.

113
00:10:16,670 --> 00:10:17,850
And you too, Commander.

114
00:10:18,520 --> 00:10:20,270
The emperor called you too.

115
00:10:33,890 --> 00:10:35,860
With your permission, Turgut Bey.

116
00:10:46,980 --> 00:10:48,320
Öktem Bey.

117
00:10:49,010 --> 00:10:52,760
They will kill all these warriors
with your word.

118
00:10:53,030 --> 00:10:54,590
Turgut Bey is right.

119
00:10:56,300 --> 00:10:58,210
The blood spilled
will be our blood.

120
00:11:02,920 --> 00:11:04,390
Give up.

121
00:11:05,850 --> 00:11:07,640
We are behind you.

122
00:11:20,460 --> 00:11:21,880
Alps!

123
00:11:41,650 --> 00:11:43,490
Put down your swords.

124
00:11:51,480 --> 00:11:53,110
You have heard your Bey.

125
00:11:54,390 --> 00:11:56,370
Put the swords in their sheaths, come on.

126
00:11:56,470 --> 00:11:57,780
Soldiers.

127
00:12:09,270 --> 00:12:10,390
Don't do it, Bey.

128
00:12:11,890 --> 00:12:16,420
Whoever puts gold in your tribe will put
the rope around your neck tomorrow.

129
00:12:18,420 --> 00:12:20,240
Put your sword down, Hatun.

130
00:12:23,520 --> 00:12:24,260
Father.

131
00:12:46,930 --> 00:12:48,290
From now on...

132
00:12:49,640 --> 00:12:51,410
It's up to you, Turgut Bey.

133
00:12:53,940 --> 00:12:55,720
For the safety of my tribe...

134
00:13:00,260 --> 00:13:03,650
I will surrender to the
justice of Osman Bey.

135
00:13:03,830 --> 00:13:06,280
Trust our scale of justice.

136
00:13:06,820 --> 00:13:08,610
You did the right thing.

137
00:13:25,350 --> 00:13:27,730
The emperor will ask me
to cut off your head.

138
00:13:27,990 --> 00:13:30,320
You caused Ophelia to escape.

139
00:13:30,790 --> 00:13:32,320
I will be your executioner.

140
00:13:32,740 --> 00:13:34,950
I will know who you serve.

141
00:13:36,420 --> 00:13:38,980
Then you will see who
will be the executioner...

142
00:13:39,380 --> 00:13:40,980
who will be the victim.

143
00:13:42,480 --> 00:13:45,780
Odin's soldiers serve only Odin.

144
00:13:46,840 --> 00:13:49,960
And the emperor, of course.

145
00:13:51,960 --> 00:13:54,040
You tricked Ophelia's mind.

146
00:13:54,310 --> 00:13:56,230
She tried to kill her father.

147
00:13:57,560 --> 00:13:59,540
The emperor knows everything.

148
00:14:00,470 --> 00:14:02,600
This will be your death decision.

149
00:14:03,560 --> 00:14:04,900
Look at me.

150
00:14:05,890 --> 00:14:08,320
Do you see a frightened man?

151
00:14:10,130 --> 00:14:12,310
Allah wrote my fate.

152
00:14:13,110 --> 00:14:15,890
I will not be afraid of the
words of an idolater like you.

153
00:14:17,080 --> 00:14:20,100
Even if Odin himself is the one
holding your ropes...

154
00:14:21,480 --> 00:14:22,660
I will find it.

155
00:14:28,200 --> 00:14:29,160
Olof.

156
00:14:34,210 --> 00:14:36,310
The emperor is waiting for you.

157
00:14:58,340 --> 00:15:00,740
May Jesus sanctify you, Sarkis.

158
00:15:01,490 --> 00:15:02,740
I was very afraid.

159
00:15:03,960 --> 00:15:05,650
What if something
happened to you?

160
00:15:07,760 --> 00:15:11,240
Was that help you talked about from Osman?

161
00:15:12,160 --> 00:15:15,060
Yes, and he did not disappoint us.

162
00:15:15,240 --> 00:15:18,210
And what about my father?
Is there any news about him?

163
00:15:18,220 --> 00:15:19,210
Is he alive?

164
00:15:19,280 --> 00:15:21,775
If something had happened
to the emperor...

165
00:15:21,785 --> 00:15:25,515
those who wanted the throne
would have already moved.

166
00:15:28,120 --> 00:15:29,170
Someone is coming.

167
00:15:29,190 --> 00:15:30,700
Don't think about it, princess.

168
00:15:30,730 --> 00:15:32,660
Your predictions may be correct

169
00:15:32,720 --> 00:15:34,560
I promise you, princess.

170
00:15:34,850 --> 00:15:37,210
I will learn your father's condition.

171
00:15:51,840 --> 00:15:53,540
You will be fine, princess.

172
00:15:55,110 --> 00:15:56,360
You and your dad too.

173
00:15:57,730 --> 00:15:59,620
I believe you Sarkis.

174
00:16:02,290 --> 00:16:04,520
Stop, don't run, stop.

175
00:16:05,400 --> 00:16:06,390
Catch them!

176
00:16:07,840 --> 00:16:09,670
I had told you, emperor.

177
00:16:11,280 --> 00:16:12,560
Be careful.

178
00:16:14,020 --> 00:16:16,560
Your position doesn't want negligence.

179
00:16:16,950 --> 00:16:20,740
How careful I can be when it
was my daughter who attacked me?

180
00:16:22,500 --> 00:16:23,460
Look at this.

181
00:16:24,360 --> 00:16:25,880
My daughter is poisoning me.

182
00:16:27,040 --> 00:16:29,250
And the enemy will save me.

183
00:16:30,070 --> 00:16:33,270
Osman who saved your life today...

184
00:16:33,880 --> 00:16:36,520
saved Ophelia, who wanted to kill you.

185
00:16:37,780 --> 00:16:39,590
You can't forgive him for this.

186
00:16:45,330 --> 00:16:47,810
Ophelia's death will be at my hands.

187
00:16:49,600 --> 00:16:51,940
But she will speak first.

188
00:16:52,360 --> 00:16:57,030
She will tell us about Frigg, the
snake on my land.

189
00:16:59,730 --> 00:17:01,940
He caused her to run away.

190
00:17:02,050 --> 00:17:03,590
He killed my men.

191
00:17:03,880 --> 00:17:06,069
From this city...

192
00:17:19,520 --> 00:17:22,800
While no one in the palace knows
that I have been poisoned...

193
00:17:23,910 --> 00:17:26,339
How do know, Osman Bey?

194
00:17:31,480 --> 00:17:33,000
And you, Olof?

195
00:17:34,480 --> 00:17:36,040
Did you know?

196
00:17:37,890 --> 00:17:38,850
I...

197
00:17:40,340 --> 00:17:45,490
I crucify anyone who even thinks of this.

198
00:17:48,320 --> 00:17:50,790
How did you know, Osman Bey?

199
00:17:50,920 --> 00:17:52,790
You're fine because I know.

200
00:17:54,230 --> 00:17:55,730
Don't check with me about this.

201
00:17:57,300 --> 00:18:03,350
The eye that watches the palace, only
covets the throne, Emperor.

202
00:18:04,100 --> 00:18:07,880
I will pluck out that eye and
present it as a gift to Odin.

203
00:18:10,280 --> 00:18:12,720
Damn! Who did this?

204
00:18:21,010 --> 00:18:22,400
It is enough.

205
00:18:33,280 --> 00:18:38,230
First it poisons me, then it
makes me better.

206
00:18:39,400 --> 00:18:41,110
Is that what you're saying, Olof?

207
00:18:44,290 --> 00:18:45,800
And what about Frigg?

208
00:18:46,850 --> 00:18:47,800
Ophelia?

209
00:18:49,190 --> 00:18:51,720
Did you know about them
thanks to your spies?

210
00:18:52,210 --> 00:18:53,160
No.

211
00:18:54,530 --> 00:18:56,210
Kantakuzenos told me.

212
00:18:57,000 --> 00:19:03,590
Ophelia has sent a spy called Frigg to
my land to wreak havoc.

213
00:19:04,200 --> 00:19:06,210
First, she will talk about this.

214
00:19:07,680 --> 00:19:11,600
But Olof wants to kill her.

215
00:19:12,550 --> 00:19:15,830
It was my daughter who attacked
you and me, Osman Bey.

216
00:19:15,880 --> 00:19:19,520
But the throne is not managed by mercy.

217
00:19:20,050 --> 00:19:22,370
She will be killed as soon as she is seen.

218
00:19:22,410 --> 00:19:26,800
No one will die before I hear what I want.

219
00:19:28,230 --> 00:19:33,220
The sedition on your land has
reached my land.

220
00:19:33,410 --> 00:19:35,220
Frigg is on your land now.

221
00:19:36,310 --> 00:19:38,180
And Ophelia will go there.

222
00:19:39,360 --> 00:19:40,840
I will kill her.

223
00:19:41,830 --> 00:19:44,870
You won't get between me
and my daughter, Osman Bey.

224
00:19:44,870 --> 00:19:48,630
My land, my matter.

225
00:19:51,890 --> 00:19:56,630
I'll give you your daughter after
I take what I want...

226
00:19:59,080 --> 00:20:01,120
my friend Andronikos.

227
00:20:05,190 --> 00:20:07,590
Be my guest tonight, Osman Bey.

228
00:20:08,560 --> 00:20:11,080
We haven't finished talking yet.

229
00:20:11,750 --> 00:20:13,080
Thank you, Emperor!

230
00:20:14,880 --> 00:20:16,580
Excuse me now.

231
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:44,370
What is this, brother?

232
00:20:48,740 --> 00:20:52,560
Greek gold!

233
00:20:56,070 --> 00:20:57,010
What happened?

234
00:21:00,630 --> 00:21:04,450
Please friends, don't stop until
you reach Yenişehir.

235
00:21:07,200 --> 00:21:09,570
What's happening? What's going ON?

236
00:21:10,400 --> 00:21:12,670
Come on, Cerkutay, come on.

237
00:21:12,840 --> 00:21:14,140
Come on, Cerkutay.

238
00:21:14,600 --> 00:21:16,020
Kantakuzenos.

239
00:21:18,290 --> 00:21:19,890
Your wound is deep, Kantakuzenos.

240
00:21:21,140 --> 00:21:23,520
Come with us to host you in Yenişehir.

241
00:21:25,520 --> 00:21:28,840
If I didn't destroy the tribe over the
heads of these rude ones...

242
00:21:29,560 --> 00:21:31,520
It was because of my trust in you.

243
00:21:32,040 --> 00:21:35,000
If the balance of your
justice is spoiled...

244
00:21:35,440 --> 00:21:39,140
know that I will not hesitate
to apply my justice.

245
00:21:41,140 --> 00:21:44,160
Calm, Kantakuzenos.

246
00:21:50,440 --> 00:21:51,350
Hatun.

247
00:22:02,340 --> 00:22:03,860
Don't worry, Hatun.

248
00:22:05,510 --> 00:22:06,820
Öktem Bey.

249
00:22:08,480 --> 00:22:10,150
Let's go, Turgut Bey.

250
00:22:16,100 --> 00:22:20,690
Our soldiers will stay in the tribe until
the last moment after we're gone.

251
00:22:21,880 --> 00:22:25,010
Don't make mistakes and don't rebel.

252
00:22:25,320 --> 00:22:27,010
Nothing like this will happen.

253
00:22:31,090 --> 00:22:33,320
What you say will happen, Bey.

254
00:22:33,590 --> 00:22:35,750
However, Turgut Bey...

255
00:22:36,560 --> 00:22:40,770
if Osman Bey does any injustice...

256
00:22:41,170 --> 00:22:43,410
and if you are blinded to the truth...

257
00:22:44,560 --> 00:22:48,370
then you won't be able to stop
us even if you all come.

258
00:22:51,800 --> 00:22:56,000
The balance of justice isn't
spoiled, don't worry, Bengi Hatun.

259
00:22:59,080 --> 00:22:59,800
Let's go.

260
00:23:03,280 --> 00:23:05,620
Come on, Kantakuzenos.

261
00:23:07,950 --> 00:23:10,860
I will hold you accountable for what
we are experiencing now.

262
00:23:10,860 --> 00:23:12,130
I won't ignore it.

263
00:23:12,740 --> 00:23:13,990
Don't forget this day.

264
00:23:14,240 --> 00:23:16,660
There is nothing that we
can not account for.

265
00:23:16,770 --> 00:23:19,490
Our place and our homeland are
clear, come when you want.

266
00:23:27,300 --> 00:23:28,580
Come on.

267
00:23:39,810 --> 00:23:43,240
The days will surely come when we will
hold them accountable.

268
00:23:44,920 --> 00:23:47,210
However, we will not forget those...

269
00:23:47,220 --> 00:23:51,370
who pretended to be by our side and
didn't defend us with their swords.

270
00:23:52,590 --> 00:23:54,270
Bengi hatun.

271
00:23:55,480 --> 00:24:02,230
Do you think we didn't stand behind Öktem
Bey because we let them take him?

272
00:24:05,840 --> 00:24:11,110
If they try to sacrifice Öktem Bey
because of the infidel's game...

273
00:24:11,530 --> 00:24:16,210
we will go to Yenişehir and take it from
them by force.

274
00:24:35,780 --> 00:24:37,580
Osman Bey.

275
00:24:45,380 --> 00:24:49,620
Whenever we meet, we stand
up to each other.

276
00:24:50,740 --> 00:24:54,300
We will know who is the traitor
and who is the friend.

277
00:24:55,010 --> 00:24:57,920
And when I know this,
I will do what I have to do.

278
00:25:02,430 --> 00:25:05,140
I can control my axe.

279
00:25:05,610 --> 00:25:09,340
But if my anger controls me...

280
00:25:12,070 --> 00:25:14,720
It is my axe that rules me.

281
00:25:16,710 --> 00:25:19,830
When I got to the ring, I
went in to kill everyone.

282
00:25:20,260 --> 00:25:23,430
I didn't know we were in the same place.

283
00:25:24,170 --> 00:25:27,120
But when sinners fall into my hands...

284
00:25:29,050 --> 00:25:32,720
my axe will cut many heads.

285
00:25:35,760 --> 00:25:37,670
However, today...

286
00:25:43,420 --> 00:25:46,610
please accept my apologies, Osman Bey.

287
00:25:54,360 --> 00:25:56,920
An apology is the hallmark of the brave.

288
00:25:58,310 --> 00:26:02,450
But forgiveness is an attribute
of the strong.

289
00:26:11,910 --> 00:26:16,150
The smell of innocent blood is still on
your hand that you hold for peace.

290
00:26:18,400 --> 00:26:21,070
A warrior's hand must be
stained with blood.

291
00:26:21,920 --> 00:26:24,920
There was no innocent person
among those ı killed.

292
00:26:26,160 --> 00:26:30,620
I hope we never meet again as enemies.

293
00:26:31,100 --> 00:26:33,220
I say this for your safety.

294
00:26:33,900 --> 00:26:39,650
When the time comes, we will see
who is innocent and who is guilty.

295
00:26:58,870 --> 00:27:01,860
- Was he sincerely asking for forgiveness?
- No.

296
00:27:02,490 --> 00:27:05,510
He's trying to make me lower my shield.

297
00:27:06,660 --> 00:27:08,720
But that's part of the game.

298
00:27:12,050 --> 00:27:14,000
I will definitely kill him.

299
00:27:15,530 --> 00:27:18,260
We carry healing and
death within us as well.

300
00:27:20,740 --> 00:27:23,340
- Are you going to do this in the palace, my Bey?
- I won't go.

301
00:27:24,420 --> 00:27:27,200
He's coming to kill me.

302
00:27:27,530 --> 00:27:31,310
But not in the palace, but
in the place I want.

303
00:27:32,450 --> 00:27:35,030
I will find out who he serves to...

304
00:27:35,130 --> 00:27:39,290
and then I will hang his body at
the gate of Constantinople.

305
00:27:42,610 --> 00:27:45,870
Osman will not stop.

306
00:27:45,970 --> 00:27:48,410
You will follow his footsteps
like a shadow.

307
00:27:48,740 --> 00:27:50,500
What's on your mind, Olof?

308
00:27:54,570 --> 00:27:56,740
The gods want an offering. (sacrifice)

309
00:27:57,360 --> 00:28:00,730
But I want revenge.
Both will happen.

310
00:28:01,490 --> 00:28:06,220
Osman will die when he leaves the palace.

311
00:28:09,750 --> 00:28:14,000
Would killing Osman make
the emperor our enemy?

312
00:28:15,120 --> 00:28:18,560
I make whoever I want our enemy.

313
00:28:19,110 --> 00:28:23,210
But it is not me who will kill
Osman, but Ophelia.

314
00:28:27,330 --> 00:28:29,500
Ophelia the Demon.

315
00:28:29,710 --> 00:28:34,370
She's such a demon that she
poisoned her father first...

316
00:28:35,200 --> 00:28:38,010
then she killed Osman.

317
00:28:40,990 --> 00:28:43,230
There are people who are worse
than us, Frodi.

318
00:28:43,480 --> 00:28:45,840
There are people
who are worse than us.

319
00:28:51,620 --> 00:28:53,640
Yenişehir

320
00:29:09,740 --> 00:29:12,690
Kantakuzenos has a deep
wound, Malhun Hatun.

321
00:29:12,810 --> 00:29:15,085
His condition got worse while
we came here.

322
00:29:15,095 --> 00:29:18,075
It would be good to get the
doctors to treat him.

323
00:29:18,640 --> 00:29:23,290
Alps, prepare the guest hall immediately
and tell the doctors (healers) to come.

324
00:29:41,580 --> 00:29:44,450
Come on, give it up right away.

325
00:29:47,820 --> 00:29:50,280
My wound is a minor wound, and
there is no need to worry.

326
00:29:50,550 --> 00:29:52,590
The doctors will decide that.

327
00:29:53,840 --> 00:29:55,710
Come on, then.

328
00:30:21,610 --> 00:30:23,270
Marta.

329
00:30:26,740 --> 00:30:28,370
Malhun Hatun.

330
00:30:32,560 --> 00:30:34,560
How is your hand?

331
00:30:38,450 --> 00:30:40,920
It's better now, thank you.

332
00:30:41,680 --> 00:30:44,430
We have brought the last
pieces of cloth needed.

333
00:30:46,100 --> 00:30:47,880
How are you?

334
00:30:49,140 --> 00:30:52,250
Is the city safe, Malhun Hatun?

335
00:30:55,120 --> 00:30:58,940
Actually I'm not used to this, and
I feel a little scared.

336
00:31:02,910 --> 00:31:04,960
We have so many enemies, Marta.

337
00:31:06,050 --> 00:31:10,270
However, our courage will
overcome them all.

338
00:31:12,620 --> 00:31:14,780
Don't be so afraid.

339
00:31:15,050 --> 00:31:16,980
Why are you so afraid?

340
00:31:21,790 --> 00:31:24,350
Constantinople

341
00:31:34,150 --> 00:31:36,610
Come here.

342
00:31:40,480 --> 00:31:42,340
My brothers.

343
00:31:43,850 --> 00:31:45,750
Tell me! Is exile difficult?

344
00:31:45,920 --> 00:31:48,210
There is nothing difficult
about this, my Bey.

345
00:31:48,870 --> 00:31:52,310
We know how important our job is
and we're watching Emperor.

346
00:31:53,330 --> 00:31:58,200
We will always watch this fool so that
our path to conquests is always paved.

347
00:31:59,100 --> 00:32:01,850
The valiants are on
guard in East and West.

348
00:32:02,230 --> 00:32:05,480
Whoever has solid intelligence
holds the reins of power in his hand.

349
00:32:08,940 --> 00:32:12,870
This place is the source
of the strife that exists on our lands.

350
00:32:13,830 --> 00:32:18,510
But exile is the way to home.

351
00:32:19,330 --> 00:32:22,880
So tell me, what is Ophelia's condition?

352
00:32:25,230 --> 00:32:26,980
She's scared.

353
00:32:28,320 --> 00:32:30,470
She is accused of
trying to kill her father.

354
00:32:31,670 --> 00:32:33,910
But I don't know if she did that or not.

355
00:32:34,760 --> 00:32:36,570
There is no importance to that.

356
00:32:36,930 --> 00:32:39,340
Olof and the Emperor want her dead.

357
00:32:39,970 --> 00:32:42,160
It is important that we have her.

358
00:32:43,440 --> 00:32:47,525
We will take her with us on
our return to Yenişehir...

359
00:32:47,575 --> 00:32:50,685
so that we know if she is
innocent or guilty.

360
00:32:50,790 --> 00:32:54,650
The princess has been with
me for a long time, my Bey.

361
00:32:56,450 --> 00:33:00,080
And if you ask me what I see, she is
a victim, not an oppressor.

362
00:33:00,160 --> 00:33:04,700
No, this is not the time when we will
depend on what we see or hear.

363
00:33:06,520 --> 00:33:09,490
If we're going to depend on what we see...

364
00:33:09,610 --> 00:33:14,600
I should behead
Öktem Bey.

365
00:33:27,010 --> 00:33:29,600
Open the door, brother.

366
00:33:43,380 --> 00:33:45,720
We were together.

367
00:33:46,780 --> 00:33:49,530
We fought the infidels together.

368
00:33:51,450 --> 00:33:54,720
Now, you're throwing me in your cell.

369
00:33:56,430 --> 00:33:58,140
Thank you.

370
00:34:00,260 --> 00:34:03,405
If a Turkmen is hurt...

371
00:34:03,445 --> 00:34:06,955
we are the ones who will fall, Öktem Bey.

372
00:34:07,280 --> 00:34:10,090
Our pain is one, our grief is one.

373
00:34:10,630 --> 00:34:15,100
However, we have to secure the justice.

374
00:34:24,760 --> 00:34:29,100
You can't keep people inside
your dungeons, Boran.

375
00:34:30,250 --> 00:34:33,989
But now you give me a lot of advice.

376
00:34:35,750 --> 00:34:39,429
There is no justice that
can be trusted, Boran.

377
00:34:42,639 --> 00:34:48,929
Öktem Bey, we show you respect even
though all the evidence is against you.

378
00:34:49,840 --> 00:34:55,510
However, you have to know your
limit and your position well.

379
00:35:03,250 --> 00:35:07,340
You believe the accusations.

380
00:35:09,920 --> 00:35:13,730
I will bear all these slanders but...

381
00:35:14,720 --> 00:35:17,550
you got your hands dirty with
these false slanders anyway.

382
00:35:21,890 --> 00:35:23,850
Sufficient for us is Allah.

383
00:35:23,980 --> 00:35:25,080
Öktem Bey.

384
00:35:32,460 --> 00:35:37,080
So, we wash our hands with the blood of
the one who stained us with these slanders.

385
00:35:39,420 --> 00:35:42,200
First prove your innocence.

386
00:35:43,730 --> 00:35:45,420
Inshallah.

387
00:36:01,280 --> 00:36:02,790
Come on, brother.

388
00:36:11,690 --> 00:36:13,070
Brother.

389
00:36:14,700 --> 00:36:17,260
I don't hear anything and
I don't understand.

390
00:36:18,550 --> 00:36:20,530
But what I see hurts my heart.

391
00:36:21,270 --> 00:36:23,810
What's going on, brother?

392
00:36:27,710 --> 00:36:30,460
They say that there is
good in all evil, Cerkutay.

393
00:36:32,280 --> 00:36:34,590
I wish I could be in your place now, brother.

394
00:36:35,620 --> 00:36:37,280
You don't hear a word.

395
00:36:41,530 --> 00:36:43,190
It is true what you say, my brother.

396
00:36:43,430 --> 00:36:46,140
A warrior can't stay without
food or horse.

397
00:36:48,520 --> 00:36:50,420
Oh.

398
00:36:53,930 --> 00:36:54,910
Cerkutay.

399
00:36:55,080 --> 00:36:57,250
Don't you really hear, brother?

400
00:36:57,690 --> 00:36:59,380
Or are you playing a game on me?

401
00:37:04,760 --> 00:37:05,970
No, no.

402
00:37:08,070 --> 00:37:09,440
You don't really hear.

403
00:37:10,320 --> 00:37:11,910
Come on brother, come on.

404
00:37:16,730 --> 00:37:17,800
tell me.

405
00:37:18,020 --> 00:37:19,310
How did this wound happen?

406
00:37:21,400 --> 00:37:22,650
It's a serious wound.

407
00:37:23,400 --> 00:37:24,900
But it doesn't hurt.

408
00:37:25,430 --> 00:37:26,960
It makes me weak.

409
00:37:28,790 --> 00:37:30,400
It's very difficult.

410
00:37:31,400 --> 00:37:33,160
What is difficult, my Bey?

411
00:37:33,530 --> 00:37:36,310
I went through all these wars
and was not affected.

412
00:37:38,660 --> 00:37:39,880
You know.

413
00:37:43,380 --> 00:37:45,200
Shall I say?

414
00:37:47,340 --> 00:37:48,600
It's a heart wound.

415
00:37:51,440 --> 00:37:54,300
Wait, I'll boil you soup.
It'll do you good.

416
00:37:54,970 --> 00:37:58,170
But you will suffer a lot.

417
00:37:58,710 --> 00:38:00,450
What are you looking at, my Bey?

418
00:38:01,220 --> 00:38:03,990
Love is a test.

419
00:38:04,560 --> 00:38:05,890
Either you love her...

420
00:38:07,840 --> 00:38:09,360
and she doesn't love you...

421
00:38:12,430 --> 00:38:14,260
Or you two love each other...

422
00:38:14,440 --> 00:38:17,250
And this time, various misfortunes
come and befall you.

423
00:38:19,310 --> 00:38:21,240
Love crushes us.

424
00:38:24,190 --> 00:38:25,600
It is true what you say.

425
00:38:26,270 --> 00:38:28,200
But I insist, Ülgen Hatun.

426
00:38:30,610 --> 00:38:32,300
On this bumpy road...

427
00:38:32,780 --> 00:38:34,580
I'll walk until my feet bleed.

428
00:38:34,810 --> 00:38:37,820
Inshallah, walk. Let the paths be yours.

429
00:38:38,400 --> 00:38:41,940
But, tell me first. You were in the tribe
all that time.

430
00:38:42,120 --> 00:38:44,740
Did you talk to the girl? Is
she interested?

431
00:38:46,540 --> 00:38:47,640
I do not know.

432
00:38:48,800 --> 00:38:53,020
She didn't even say my name.

433
00:38:53,070 --> 00:38:54,130
Don't say that.

434
00:38:55,020 --> 00:38:57,560
Fire fell in the heart of the Alçiçek.

435
00:39:03,170 --> 00:39:04,210
Subasi.

436
00:39:06,830 --> 00:39:08,220
Welcome, Bala Hatun.

437
00:39:09,900 --> 00:39:12,490
Things got complicated in
Yenişehir in your absence.

438
00:39:12,910 --> 00:39:14,350
The system is new.

439
00:39:14,840 --> 00:39:16,760
But you must take precautions first.

440
00:39:17,190 --> 00:39:20,810
Are things to get complicated in
Yenişehir because you are not there?

441
00:39:21,900 --> 00:39:23,500
I scolded all the Alps.

442
00:39:23,580 --> 00:39:26,050
The number of Alps in dungeon increased.

443
00:39:26,260 --> 00:39:28,630
Nothing like this will
happen again, Inshallah.

444
00:39:29,000 --> 00:39:30,050
Good.

445
00:39:30,950 --> 00:39:33,040
But something comes to my mind.

446
00:39:34,670 --> 00:39:37,210
You increased the number of
Alps in dungeon earlier.

447
00:39:38,050 --> 00:39:39,490
What is the reason for this?

448
00:39:40,600 --> 00:39:43,850
Was there an intrusion attempt
that we don't know about?

449
00:39:48,070 --> 00:39:50,710
Is there anything you would
like to say, Subasi?

450
00:39:57,260 --> 00:40:01,380
The girl entered Osman Bey's dungeon...

451
00:40:01,600 --> 00:40:03,430
and wounded Subasi...

452
00:40:03,740 --> 00:40:07,030
then she got out and went as
if nothing had happened, right?

453
00:40:08,380 --> 00:40:10,370
Which girl hurt you?

454
00:40:10,990 --> 00:40:13,010
Alçiçek?

455
00:40:19,890 --> 00:40:22,020
You represent justice...

456
00:40:22,590 --> 00:40:24,840
and form the system, Subasi.

457
00:40:26,830 --> 00:40:29,740
If you did it, what would
the warriors do?

458
00:40:30,050 --> 00:40:31,500
Well, you did this.

459
00:40:32,280 --> 00:40:33,710
You made this mistake.

460
00:40:34,570 --> 00:40:36,150
How do you hide this?

461
00:40:38,770 --> 00:40:42,960
Alçiçek was very angry because
of what happened to her uncle.

462
00:40:43,210 --> 00:40:45,330
However, before...

463
00:40:45,400 --> 00:40:47,070
She tried to kill you, Aktemur.

464
00:40:47,860 --> 00:40:49,340
Is there more than this?

465
00:40:53,660 --> 00:40:55,730
She didn't try to kill me, Bala Hatun.

466
00:40:56,970 --> 00:40:58,190
It's a small wound.

467
00:40:58,980 --> 00:41:01,060
It went wrong when I tried to block it.

468
00:41:01,130 --> 00:41:03,900
In that mission, you are not Aktemur.

469
00:41:04,130 --> 00:41:05,200
You are the Subasi.

470
00:41:05,780 --> 00:41:09,570
Whoever tried to kill you
tried to corrupt Yenişehir.

471
00:41:21,640 --> 00:41:23,620
You're blind.

472
00:41:24,280 --> 00:41:27,010
The girl tried to kill you.

473
00:41:29,260 --> 00:41:33,950
Is that girl more important
than your life and your job?

474
00:41:34,080 --> 00:41:34,910
Mother.

475
00:41:36,480 --> 00:41:38,500
I don't put anyone before my job.

476
00:41:38,580 --> 00:41:39,670
Yeah, I saw it.

477
00:41:41,500 --> 00:41:44,560
Is that why you protect the girl
who tried to kill you?

478
00:42:04,590 --> 00:42:06,290
It's the lane map.

479
00:42:10,850 --> 00:42:13,720
Tell me, what's Olof doing?

480
00:42:13,800 --> 00:42:15,540
We watched him.

481
00:42:15,660 --> 00:42:17,940
He sets up a trap with his soldiers.

482
00:42:22,300 --> 00:42:24,060
There are few soldiers here.

483
00:42:25,360 --> 00:42:27,070
It is suitable for trap.

484
00:42:29,680 --> 00:42:31,620
He will attack here.

485
00:42:32,970 --> 00:42:34,470
He will come for you, my Bey.

486
00:42:38,750 --> 00:42:40,040
We'll take Olof tonight...

487
00:42:40,410 --> 00:42:42,720
and we know for whom he works.

488
00:42:43,110 --> 00:42:46,200
The source of his courage is
knowing that I'm alone here.

489
00:42:47,730 --> 00:42:50,100
He won't stop until he gets what he wants.

490
00:42:51,050 --> 00:42:52,790
Even exile is a home for us.

491
00:42:53,230 --> 00:42:55,330
Turks will never be alone.

492
00:42:59,800 --> 00:43:01,200
Don't hide.

493
00:43:02,560 --> 00:43:04,000
You can show up.

494
00:43:20,160 --> 00:43:21,910
Merchant Vassilis.

495
00:43:22,770 --> 00:43:24,320
Hasan Alp, my Bey.

496
00:43:25,320 --> 00:43:26,680
Waiting for your order.

497
00:43:29,860 --> 00:43:31,100
Maid Hera.

498
00:43:32,510 --> 00:43:35,090
Sister Gökçe is at your
command, Osman Bey.

499
00:43:36,310 --> 00:43:40,770
They are the fruits of the seeds
that we planted years ago.

500
00:43:41,980 --> 00:43:45,940
These formations are older than our age.

501
00:43:47,330 --> 00:43:51,920
It will add strength to our
strength for generations, Inshallah.

502
00:43:52,490 --> 00:43:55,160
I have three sons.

503
00:43:55,410 --> 00:43:58,600
I raised them all to serve the country.

504
00:43:59,060 --> 00:44:00,410
Mashallah!

505
00:44:00,840 --> 00:44:02,720
Even if we are in the peace period...

506
00:44:02,770 --> 00:44:05,290
do not take your eyes off the enemy.

507
00:44:06,080 --> 00:44:07,470
Thank you.

508
00:44:08,470 --> 00:44:10,850
It's time to pluck out the enemy's eye.

509
00:44:11,810 --> 00:44:13,500
Start the preparations.

510
00:44:24,330 --> 00:44:26,280
Öktem tribe

511
00:44:35,580 --> 00:44:37,170
The great Beys of my tribe...

512
00:44:38,430 --> 00:44:41,600
We came to this frontier to conquer.

513
00:44:41,990 --> 00:44:47,750
However, they want to sacrifice our Bey
for the treacherous games of the enemy.

514
00:44:48,710 --> 00:44:50,460
You know your Bey very well.

515
00:44:51,680 --> 00:44:55,870
For the safety of his tribe, he remained
silent despite this slander...

516
00:44:56,630 --> 00:44:58,010
and surrendered himself.

517
00:44:59,250 --> 00:45:01,320
He is silent.

518
00:45:02,610 --> 00:45:04,110
But I'm not silent.

519
00:45:05,300 --> 00:45:09,090
I will not throw my Bey into the
fire that the infidels set.

520
00:45:10,700 --> 00:45:12,430
Many of our Alps...

521
00:45:13,260 --> 00:45:14,850
our valiants...

522
00:45:16,050 --> 00:45:19,180
and now this slander!

523
00:45:19,510 --> 00:45:21,890
The infidels entered among us...

524
00:45:22,110 --> 00:45:24,620
and they stained our
land with their dirty gold!

525
00:45:27,870 --> 00:45:28,860
Osman.

526
00:45:31,420 --> 00:45:33,230
Osman.

527
00:45:35,810 --> 00:45:37,470
If Osman works...

528
00:45:37,970 --> 00:45:40,990
with the infidels to get a
place with the Emperor...

529
00:45:42,210 --> 00:45:45,950
and tries to punish Öktem Bey, his
comrade in war...

530
00:45:46,770 --> 00:45:49,750
then no one will be able to stop me.

531
00:45:51,160 --> 00:45:55,610
I will collapse that land!

532
00:46:03,410 --> 00:46:06,460
With or without you!

533
00:46:09,960 --> 00:46:13,290
My Beys, going down
this road takes courage.

534
00:46:14,100 --> 00:46:18,700
The end of this path is not obeying Osman's orders...

535
00:46:18,870 --> 00:46:20,430
and rebellion.

536
00:46:21,780 --> 00:46:24,640
Even if there is only one
person behind me...

537
00:46:24,830 --> 00:46:26,650
I'm going this way.

538
00:46:29,790 --> 00:46:31,660
And now I ask you...

539
00:46:33,310 --> 00:46:37,750
When the time comes and I draw my sword...

540
00:46:39,190 --> 00:46:41,420
Will you be by my side?

541
00:46:45,020 --> 00:46:47,130
Or will you stand against me?

542
00:46:52,380 --> 00:46:54,160
We are with you, Bengi Hatun.

543
00:46:55,490 --> 00:46:57,050
We keep our words.

544
00:46:57,310 --> 00:46:59,310
We will not leave
Öktem Bey alone.

545
00:47:01,510 --> 00:47:06,100
Let Osman Bey think about the rest.

546
00:47:24,010 --> 00:47:25,250
Mother.

547
00:47:29,190 --> 00:47:31,790
I wish we waited for court first.

548
00:47:32,720 --> 00:47:34,700
Osman Bey trusts my father.

549
00:47:35,090 --> 00:47:36,350
- Now...
- Alçiçek!

550
00:47:39,510 --> 00:47:41,260
What are you saying?

551
00:47:41,650 --> 00:47:43,050
What are you saying?

552
00:47:44,600 --> 00:47:48,350
Why do you sit aside
and remain silent?

553
00:47:50,090 --> 00:47:51,820
They killed your uncle.

554
00:47:52,850 --> 00:47:55,120
They are about to kill your father.

555
00:47:56,060 --> 00:48:02,890
Will you send your father to death?

556
00:48:05,880 --> 00:48:07,170
We won't send, mother.

557
00:48:18,920 --> 00:48:20,770
Since Osman Bey won't come...

558
00:48:20,810 --> 00:48:23,330
It makes no sense for me
to stay here any longer.

559
00:48:25,170 --> 00:48:26,430
I will go.

560
00:48:26,600 --> 00:48:28,160
just chill.

561
00:48:29,220 --> 00:48:32,560
We won't let you go anywhere
while you're like this, you know.

562
00:48:32,830 --> 00:48:36,540
But I also know you
don't stick to your words.

563
00:48:38,300 --> 00:48:42,320
Osman Bey is sending me to the
Öktem tribe and he is not there.

564
00:48:42,490 --> 00:48:43,470
Where is he?

565
00:48:44,040 --> 00:48:47,100
If Osman Bey wanted this, you
would have known where he is.

566
00:48:48,170 --> 00:48:51,390
What you know is enough.

567
00:48:51,500 --> 00:48:53,580
If you have another
request, let us know.

568
00:48:53,620 --> 00:48:54,980
Until then...

569
00:48:57,230 --> 00:48:58,790
You are our guest.

570
00:49:00,870 --> 00:49:04,970
In that case, I want you to bring
me the best cloth seller in your city.

571
00:49:05,350 --> 00:49:07,850
At least I will get rid of these clothes.

572
00:49:08,650 --> 00:49:10,250
Okay.

573
00:49:27,620 --> 00:49:30,820
So, Bengi Hatun gathers Beys.

574
00:49:33,880 --> 00:49:36,210
The split is coming soon.

575
00:49:39,400 --> 00:49:44,520
Now, Osman has a big wound.

576
00:49:44,780 --> 00:49:46,500
He has, my Bey.

577
00:49:46,720 --> 00:49:49,540
Shall I make this
wound bleed?

578
00:49:49,620 --> 00:49:51,440
We did what you said, my Bey.

579
00:49:51,780 --> 00:49:52,780
You did.

580
00:49:58,470 --> 00:49:59,990
You did your job well.

581
00:50:00,250 --> 00:50:01,730
Now, it's my turn.

582
00:50:14,800 --> 00:50:17,240
I buried the man in the
middle of the tent, my Bey.

583
00:50:17,250 --> 00:50:18,160
Good.

584
00:50:19,160 --> 00:50:22,570
In due time, get him out of the place
where you buried him...

585
00:50:22,960 --> 00:50:24,610
and get rid of it.

586
00:50:25,130 --> 00:50:26,590
Your order, my Bey.

587
00:50:27,160 --> 00:50:29,230
But since we can kill him...

588
00:50:29,470 --> 00:50:31,240
Why do we hurt him, my Bey?

589
00:50:31,240 --> 00:50:33,190
To rub that wound.

590
00:50:34,180 --> 00:50:36,070
Put this in your mind.

591
00:50:37,310 --> 00:50:41,050
I don't care to gather strength.

592
00:50:41,820 --> 00:50:45,460
I want to collect gold.

593
00:50:45,870 --> 00:50:47,960
Let them fight.

594
00:50:48,050 --> 00:50:51,680
So that they will ruin their reputation.

595
00:50:51,920 --> 00:50:54,420
Merchants will come and find me.

596
00:50:55,380 --> 00:50:59,840
I will get a lot of gold out of that wound.

597
00:51:03,340 --> 00:51:05,140
Understood, right, Huseyin?

598
00:51:05,520 --> 00:51:07,420
I understand, I understand, my Bey.

599
00:51:07,540 --> 00:51:08,680
Good.

600
00:51:10,010 --> 00:51:16,150
Now I'll take the gold that
came out of the Öktem tribe.

601
00:51:17,520 --> 00:51:20,840
Find me reliable men quickly.

602
00:51:21,610 --> 00:51:24,400
I will not let the infidels get that gold.

603
00:51:24,670 --> 00:51:25,510
Hüseyin.

604
00:51:25,810 --> 00:51:26,960
Your order, my Bey.

605
00:51:27,120 --> 00:51:29,650
If you come before you find that gold...

606
00:51:31,140 --> 00:51:32,850
don't let me see you.

607
00:51:33,540 --> 00:51:35,280
Your order, my Bey.

608
00:51:46,300 --> 00:51:49,150
Constantinople
Emperor's Palace

609
00:52:02,120 --> 00:52:03,860
Constantinople.

610
00:52:15,380 --> 00:52:16,710
My Bey.

611
00:52:18,330 --> 00:52:20,540
I understand everything but...

612
00:52:21,430 --> 00:52:23,100
What is your primary goal?

613
00:52:23,960 --> 00:52:25,500
My goal...

614
00:52:25,780 --> 00:52:30,180
is to set foot in the land of the infidels.

615
00:52:34,330 --> 00:52:37,800
My goal is to make the banner
of Islam fly all over the world.

616
00:52:43,620 --> 00:52:46,770
That's why you protect the emperor.

617
00:52:47,090 --> 00:52:48,560
No.

618
00:52:50,090 --> 00:52:51,950
I don't just protect the emperor.

619
00:52:53,210 --> 00:52:55,120
I use him.

620
00:52:55,800 --> 00:53:00,050
I even interfere in state affairs.

621
00:53:02,280 --> 00:53:03,880
I keep the enemy by my side.

622
00:53:04,650 --> 00:53:06,050
I keep them by my side...

623
00:53:06,450 --> 00:53:09,470
to have a chance to spoil this
game when the time comes.

624
00:53:10,200 --> 00:53:12,980
We will be fine.

625
00:53:13,820 --> 00:53:16,210
Our goal is the emperor, Osman

626
00:53:16,230 --> 00:53:17,770
The emperor.

627
00:53:19,390 --> 00:53:23,030
The emperor sits on the throne
as long as we want.

628
00:53:24,050 --> 00:53:25,760
Our goal is Byzantium.

629
00:53:26,310 --> 00:53:28,010
Our goal will be great.

630
00:53:28,290 --> 00:53:30,700
So that we will be great too.

631
00:53:31,560 --> 00:53:33,230
We will crush the Byzantines.

632
00:53:33,740 --> 00:53:35,690
And we will become a state, Inshallah.

633
00:53:39,290 --> 00:53:41,860
I heard you were up to
something, Bengi Hatun.

634
00:53:41,930 --> 00:53:44,490
What is happening here? Why
did you gather the Beys?

635
00:53:44,550 --> 00:53:46,850
Why did you come, Malhun Hatun?

636
00:53:47,340 --> 00:53:50,050
Turgut Bey harmed my tribe.

637
00:53:50,100 --> 00:53:52,280
Do you want to harm the rest?

638
00:53:52,350 --> 00:53:54,590
No, Bengi Hatun.

639
00:53:55,170 --> 00:53:56,910
I came to share your pain.

640
00:53:57,330 --> 00:54:01,690
But I didn't like what I
saw or what I heard.

641
00:54:01,770 --> 00:54:03,250
You say we hurt...

642
00:54:03,860 --> 00:54:05,410
and we put salt on the wound.

643
00:54:05,540 --> 00:54:07,740
I don't want your mercy.

644
00:54:09,200 --> 00:54:11,810
It is clear that you are
chasing big goals.

645
00:54:12,180 --> 00:54:14,210
But I will not allow this.

646
00:54:14,670 --> 00:54:16,820
Why did you gather the Beys, Bengi Hatun?

647
00:54:16,860 --> 00:54:19,300
What is your goal? Tell the truth.

648
00:54:19,550 --> 00:54:20,690
Malhun Hatun.

649
00:54:21,940 --> 00:54:24,360
This is my tribe, this is my tent.

650
00:54:25,480 --> 00:54:28,570
I gather my Beys and Alps whenever I want.

651
00:54:30,630 --> 00:54:32,450
I don't need to consult
anyone about anything.

652
00:54:32,570 --> 00:54:33,990
You will, Hatun!

653
00:54:34,460 --> 00:54:38,850
You'll consult Osman with every move you
make for the sake of your tribe and people.

654
00:54:39,370 --> 00:54:41,530
What have we learned from
his advice to date?

655
00:54:42,240 --> 00:54:46,700
My brother is under the ground
because we listened to your words.

656
00:54:48,600 --> 00:54:52,520
My husband is in the dungeon
because we trusted you.

657
00:54:54,350 --> 00:54:59,570
From now on, I won't consult you.

658
00:55:00,650 --> 00:55:02,170
What are you implying, Hatun?

659
00:55:03,020 --> 00:55:05,070
What is our fault?

660
00:55:05,800 --> 00:55:07,750
It turns out that gold is in your tribe.

661
00:55:07,780 --> 00:55:10,720
Are we the ones who
put that gold in your tribe?

662
00:55:12,320 --> 00:55:15,670
You accuse Osman Bey for everything
happens in your tribe.

663
00:55:17,100 --> 00:55:18,970
But this anger is not good.

664
00:55:19,620 --> 00:55:22,420
This anger will make you wrong.

665
00:55:22,700 --> 00:55:25,350
It's not me who make mistakes.

666
00:55:26,050 --> 00:55:28,200
It is you who make mistakes.

667
00:55:29,400 --> 00:55:32,450
You have brought that
infidel into your palace.

668
00:55:33,350 --> 00:55:36,970
That dog's hands are stained
with the blood of a brave men.

669
00:55:39,600 --> 00:55:42,130
Instead of killing him...

670
00:55:42,250 --> 00:55:44,250
you bandaged his wounds.

671
00:55:45,700 --> 00:55:51,250
Not everyone is our
friend, Bengi Hatun.

672
00:55:51,300 --> 00:55:54,020
If we helped Kantakuzenos, we
have our reasons.

673
00:55:54,070 --> 00:55:57,640
I'm not good at politics, and I
don't like complicated business like that.

674
00:55:57,750 --> 00:56:00,350
But there is one thing I know.

675
00:56:01,900 --> 00:56:06,920
From now on, we are not on the same side.

676
00:56:09,750 --> 00:56:12,970
Okay then, Bengi Hatun.

677
00:56:13,670 --> 00:56:16,320
So, we deal with you as you said.

678
00:56:17,350 --> 00:56:19,400
My eyes will be on you until the court.

679
00:56:20,150 --> 00:56:21,700
Be careful.

680
00:56:23,270 --> 00:56:27,400
If you make one mistake, you will be
next to your husband in the dungeon.

681
00:56:32,550 --> 00:56:34,200
We'll see.

682
00:56:35,620 --> 00:56:38,150
Are you sure Olof will
come after you, my Bey?

683
00:56:38,370 --> 00:56:40,500
I'll show myself as Olof's bait.

684
00:56:40,680 --> 00:56:42,680
He will come after me.

685
00:56:43,000 --> 00:56:44,970
However, he will be the bait.

686
00:56:46,370 --> 00:56:48,170
Then I will come too, my Bey.

687
00:56:49,100 --> 00:56:50,370
No.

688
00:56:51,650 --> 00:56:54,170
You will take care of the
Emperor's health.

689
00:56:54,800 --> 00:56:56,800
This is the real trap.

690
00:56:57,950 --> 00:56:59,670
Olof will die.

691
00:56:59,720 --> 00:57:02,500
But you won't take your eyes off them.

692
00:57:04,320 --> 00:57:05,750
Okay, my Bey.

693
00:57:06,200 --> 00:57:08,050
Well.

694
00:57:11,070 --> 00:57:12,360
Come on.

695
00:57:39,350 --> 00:57:41,470
Come, Olof.

696
00:57:41,970 --> 00:57:45,320
The only place you'll follow
me to is your death.

697
00:57:55,550 --> 00:57:59,120
Olof, Osman is starting to move.

698
00:58:00,150 --> 00:58:01,700
Nice.

699
00:58:07,800 --> 00:58:11,770
Don't forget, we will kill Osman when
we see him.

700
00:58:12,400 --> 00:58:17,500
Today, our black curse will be
upon Osman...

701
00:58:18,670 --> 00:58:21,920
and then upon all the Turks, come on.

702
00:58:31,050 --> 00:58:32,600
Commander Olof!

703
00:58:32,920 --> 00:58:36,120
Emperor Andronikos is waiting for you.

704
00:58:36,650 --> 00:58:39,470
We don't want to make our emperor wait.

705
00:58:40,300 --> 00:58:42,350
But I have a thing to do.

706
00:58:43,500 --> 00:58:45,650
He is waiting, Olof.

707
00:59:00,300 --> 00:59:01,570
Frodi.

708
00:59:06,070 --> 00:59:07,900
Kill Osman.

709
00:59:08,950 --> 00:59:11,220
And let him taste the death he deserves.

710
00:59:11,240 --> 00:59:13,240
Don't worry, Olof.

711
00:59:14,520 --> 00:59:19,100
Today, Constantinople will be the
tomb of Osman.

712
00:59:34,950 --> 00:59:37,970
You should not have come
to Constantinople, Osman.

713
00:59:41,620 --> 00:59:44,270
Do everything you can.

714
00:59:57,020 --> 00:59:58,170
Now!

715
01:00:19,570 --> 01:00:23,120
Olof is listening to you, speak
up, Emperor.

716
01:00:23,620 --> 01:00:26,230
When you heard of Ophelia's betrayal...

717
01:00:26,520 --> 01:00:29,170
you took action.

718
01:00:39,770 --> 01:00:42,220
This proves your loyalty.

719
01:00:43,120 --> 01:00:48,800
Like the devotion your ancestors showed
over hundreds of years to our ruling family.

720
01:00:52,550 --> 01:00:54,320
We have always been loyal to you.

721
01:00:57,570 --> 01:01:03,300
However, you always trust the
wrong people, Emperor.

722
01:01:04,870 --> 01:01:07,120
Osman works with all of them.

723
01:01:07,200 --> 01:01:09,200
The slaves saved you that day.

724
01:01:10,550 --> 01:01:13,920
Today, they saved Ophelia, and
Osman as well.

725
01:01:15,270 --> 01:01:20,110
You can't trust anyone who
isn't noble like you.

726
01:01:20,250 --> 01:01:22,250
Are you of a noble?

727
01:01:29,500 --> 01:01:30,520
No.

728
01:01:58,950 --> 01:02:01,800
But you have the courage of
someone of noble lineage.

729
01:02:03,400 --> 01:02:07,250
No emperor, I am more
courageous than many nobles.

730
01:02:07,570 --> 01:02:11,970
You were always talking about
the demonic moves of the Turks...

731
01:02:13,650 --> 01:02:15,620
First, they open the wound...

732
01:02:16,270 --> 01:02:18,120
and then they heal it.

733
01:02:18,850 --> 01:02:21,950
In return, they gain
infinite confidence.

734
01:02:24,020 --> 01:02:25,850
Destroy that trust, Emperor.

735
01:02:25,850 --> 01:02:27,850
Tear it up.

736
01:02:28,420 --> 01:02:29,700
Trust?

737
01:02:35,300 --> 01:02:38,670
I am the emperor of Rome, Olof.

738
01:02:47,650 --> 01:02:49,920
Do you think I trust Osman?

739
01:02:51,750 --> 01:02:55,670
I'm thinking of all possibilities, that's
why you're here.

740
01:02:56,920 --> 01:02:58,720
What do you want from me?

741
01:02:59,250 --> 01:03:01,660
Ophelia must go to Osman.

742
01:03:02,100 --> 01:03:04,740
I will give you a strong unit
under your command.

743
01:03:05,520 --> 01:03:08,500
If you are right about your doubts...

744
01:03:08,650 --> 01:03:14,000
kill Ophelia and Osman.

745
01:03:15,970 --> 01:03:21,870
Your faithful servant, Olof, he'll make the
best use of this power you have given him.

746
01:03:26,270 --> 01:03:28,600
I will test Osman for
the last time tomorrow.

747
01:03:29,620 --> 01:03:32,920
And then, death to your enemies!

748
01:03:53,170 --> 01:03:54,370
Come!

749
01:04:01,220 --> 01:04:03,210
Who gives Olof commands?

750
01:04:03,370 --> 01:04:05,020
I don't know anything.

751
01:04:10,340 --> 01:04:12,450
Who is the closest person to
Olof in this mansion?

752
01:04:12,480 --> 01:04:14,280
Emperor Andronikos.

753
01:04:15,270 --> 01:04:16,940
You will speak more.

754
01:04:16,970 --> 01:04:18,500
You will speak.

755
01:04:18,550 --> 01:04:19,820
Kill me.

756
01:04:20,660 --> 01:04:21,390
Kill me.

757
01:04:21,450 --> 01:04:23,900
I decide when to kill you.

758
01:04:27,100 --> 01:04:28,320
tell me.

759
01:04:28,770 --> 01:04:30,420
Where is Olof?

760
01:04:32,450 --> 01:04:33,750
Where is Olof?

761
01:04:35,720 --> 01:04:36,570
Where?

762
01:04:46,750 --> 01:04:49,320
Soldiers, kill them all!

763
01:04:57,500 --> 01:04:59,670
It will not end here, Osman.

764
01:05:32,950 --> 01:05:34,350
Turhan.

765
01:06:10,300 --> 01:06:11,350
Osman.

766
01:06:12,170 --> 01:06:14,370
Osman was waiting for us, Olof.

767
01:06:17,770 --> 01:06:19,770
Is there a spy among you?

768
01:06:20,050 --> 01:06:21,770
How does he know?

769
01:06:25,850 --> 01:06:29,170
Thank Odin.

770
01:06:32,620 --> 01:06:34,570
You are important for Frigg.

771
01:06:38,770 --> 01:06:42,300
Otherwise, I would have cut off
your head a long time ago.

772
01:06:47,620 --> 01:06:49,070
Allow me to make it up.

773
01:06:50,870 --> 01:06:54,050
Let me kill Osman.

774
01:06:55,450 --> 01:06:57,450
Even if I would die for it...

775
01:06:58,070 --> 01:07:05,100
I will not die.
I will not die before I kill Osman.

776
01:07:06,250 --> 01:07:07,850
He is mine now.

777
01:07:09,400 --> 01:07:12,450
I will burn him alive on the land
where he was born.

778
01:07:15,350 --> 01:07:17,970
Rivers will be filled with blood.

779
01:07:17,970 --> 01:07:19,970
The soil will be wet with their blood

780
01:07:21,620 --> 01:07:23,420
I swear to Odin...

781
01:07:24,170 --> 01:07:28,720
I will run over everyone who
comes out in front of me.

782
01:07:49,420 --> 01:07:54,000
If they threw arrows at him so he wouldn't
speak, that means we got close, my Bey.

783
01:07:54,950 --> 01:07:57,570
However, they continue with
their games. (tricks)

784
01:07:58,920 --> 01:08:01,020
We will make the game even bigger.

785
01:08:01,420 --> 01:08:03,880
You will persuade Ophelia
to come to Yenişehir.

786
01:08:04,270 --> 01:08:06,770
I'll make her face Kantakuzenos.

787
01:08:08,200 --> 01:08:11,660
If she's innocent, she's in danger.

788
01:08:11,870 --> 01:08:13,870
We will protect her.

789
01:08:16,500 --> 01:08:18,550
If she's not innocent...

790
01:08:20,100 --> 01:08:22,170
I'm the one who will
hold her accountable.

791
01:08:29,800 --> 01:08:32,050
Olof will come to your land.

792
01:08:33,120 --> 01:08:37,370
I've put a unit under his command
and they're getting ready.

793
01:08:39,850 --> 01:08:43,450
Even if it is Olof who leads them, the
soldiers are my soldiers.

794
01:08:43,720 --> 01:08:46,200
I want you to host them well, Osman.

795
01:08:46,620 --> 01:08:48,420
They will find Ophelia.

796
01:08:49,000 --> 01:08:50,970
Who did you take permission from?

797
01:08:52,500 --> 01:08:54,870
I trusted our friendship, Osman Bey.

798
01:08:55,649 --> 01:08:58,200
Moreover, Ophelia is our common enemy.

799
01:08:58,229 --> 01:09:00,229
This land is under my rule.

800
01:09:01,170 --> 01:09:02,800
Ophelia is my enemy.

801
01:09:04,470 --> 01:09:06,399
But Olof is not my friend.

802
01:09:06,399 --> 01:09:11,819
Osman Bey, I will go in and
bring my enemy, even if they're in hell

803
01:09:11,819 --> 01:09:14,309
- Even if they are in your la...
- Shut up

804
01:09:14,319 --> 01:09:18,050
This land you are trying to enter
is filled with corpses of people like you.

805
01:09:19,370 --> 01:09:20,620
Osman Bey.

806
01:09:21,600 --> 01:09:24,020
Olof will stick to your words.

807
01:09:24,550 --> 01:09:28,450
And with my command, he will bring
my daughter to me.

808
01:09:28,700 --> 01:09:33,120
Have you ever obtained my permission
while entering my city?

809
01:09:33,120 --> 01:09:35,800
If we are friends, you have to prove it.

810
01:09:41,300 --> 01:09:43,220
So he'll stick to my words, huh?

811
01:09:48,569 --> 01:09:49,850
That's not enough.

812
01:09:50,250 --> 01:09:52,000
We need more than this.

813
01:09:53,370 --> 01:09:54,850
I am listening to you.

814
01:09:55,170 --> 01:09:56,400
What do you want?

815
01:09:58,070 --> 01:10:00,720
Now that we are talking
about a friendship...

816
01:10:00,950 --> 01:10:03,170
...we need to build a structure.

817
01:10:04,370 --> 01:10:08,570
I will assign the person I see fit
in that building.

818
01:10:10,750 --> 01:10:12,970
If we are talking about friendship...

819
01:10:12,970 --> 01:10:14,970
...this is how you become my friend.

820
01:10:20,720 --> 01:10:23,020
What will you gain from this, Emperor?

821
01:10:23,800 --> 01:10:26,670
The under of Emperor's palace is full of
secret passages.

822
01:10:27,520 --> 01:10:31,050
Those passages are full of demons.

823
01:10:34,450 --> 01:10:36,100
I will protect the emperor.

824
01:10:37,000 --> 01:10:39,220
There is no need for this concession.

825
01:10:40,170 --> 01:10:42,570
I'll clear the way with my axe, Emperor.

826
01:10:44,720 --> 01:10:46,350
An embassy?

827
01:10:48,070 --> 01:10:51,420
This is something that only
happens between great states.

828
01:10:53,150 --> 01:10:55,320
Are you that great?

829
01:10:56,770 --> 01:10:58,950
If we are talking about present time...

830
01:11:00,650 --> 01:11:02,920
I'm great enough for you to
owe me your life.

831
01:11:05,320 --> 01:11:07,520
But if we are talking about the past...

832
01:11:09,200 --> 01:11:12,420
We are great enough to impose taxes
on your state, as Attila did.

833
01:11:14,720 --> 01:11:16,900
As for the future, we will see it together.

834
01:11:18,100 --> 01:11:23,170
We'll see together who's the greatest.

835
01:11:25,550 --> 01:11:28,820
We always say "one for all, all for one"

836
01:11:30,170 --> 01:11:34,020
And if you don't accept this,
that means you're testing my greatness.

837
01:11:34,970 --> 01:11:37,100
Rome is here, Osman Bey.

838
01:11:37,800 --> 01:11:39,500
But where is Attila?

839
01:11:39,500 --> 01:11:41,500
You are talking to him.

840
01:11:46,700 --> 01:11:48,520
You have to agree with me.

841
01:11:58,300 --> 01:12:00,620
I will open an embassy for you, Osman bey.

842
01:12:04,220 --> 01:12:07,020
And you will open your land to Olof.

843
01:12:08,470 --> 01:12:12,550
Kantakuzenos will be busy with the trial
of Oktem Bey.

844
01:12:13,520 --> 01:12:16,950
Peace will last forever.

845
01:12:17,170 --> 01:12:20,120
No one will test the other.

846
01:12:21,520 --> 01:12:26,350
As long as you don't raise your sword,
I'll always shake your hand.

847
01:12:27,750 --> 01:12:31,120
But in the contrary case...

848
01:12:31,120 --> 01:12:36,120
I will kill whoever you send to my land.

849
01:12:40,020 --> 01:12:41,620
Emperor.

850
01:12:42,570 --> 01:12:44,490
I am going back to my hometown.

851
01:12:44,490 --> 01:12:47,720
Kumaral Abdul
will take care of your health.

852
01:12:53,950 --> 01:12:55,700
As long as we're friends...

853
01:12:57,150 --> 01:12:58,750
...I am with you.

854
01:13:12,300 --> 01:13:14,570
Yenisehir

855
01:13:26,660 --> 01:13:28,480
You have nowhere to run to anymore.

856
01:13:30,060 --> 01:13:31,320
We'll talk.

857
01:13:34,520 --> 01:13:36,710
Mother, not now.

858
01:13:37,050 --> 01:13:40,590
You cool off first, otherwise we may upset
each other.

859
01:13:40,590 --> 01:13:41,830
Aktemur!

860
01:13:42,070 --> 01:13:45,360
I say we'll talk.
So we'll talk.

861
01:13:50,730 --> 01:13:51,600
Son...

862
01:13:52,580 --> 01:13:56,100
...I know that you
fell in love with that girl.

863
01:13:59,260 --> 01:14:02,010
- Mother, you...
- Mothers always know, Aktemur!

864
01:14:02,010 --> 01:14:03,410
I know my son.

865
01:14:03,640 --> 01:14:05,760
I also see where this road leads.

866
01:14:06,160 --> 01:14:08,310
There is no end on this road!

867
01:14:08,390 --> 01:14:11,140
I don't constent to that girl, Aktemur!

868
01:14:12,280 --> 01:14:14,220
I don't want to upset you.

869
01:14:14,480 --> 01:14:17,140
But it's heart, mother.
You can't just forget.

870
01:14:17,400 --> 01:14:18,600
You have to!

871
01:14:19,250 --> 01:14:20,900
I will make you forget!

872
01:14:21,410 --> 01:14:22,240
Son.

873
01:14:23,170 --> 01:14:25,680
A lover cannot harm her lover.

874
01:14:26,030 --> 01:14:29,570
When you love someone,
you do everything to protect them.

875
01:14:30,250 --> 01:14:32,170
You do not stab him in the chest!

876
01:14:32,170 --> 01:14:33,600
It was a mistake, mother!

877
01:14:33,600 --> 01:14:34,840
Alcicek is innocent.

878
01:14:34,840 --> 01:14:36,950
I don't care whether or not!

879
01:14:37,050 --> 01:14:38,840
You will stay away from that girl.

880
01:14:39,160 --> 01:14:42,300
I will not take
that girl for you, Aktemur!

881
01:14:42,620 --> 01:14:45,120
She hurt me while trying
to protect me, mother!

882
01:14:45,120 --> 01:14:47,090
I wouldn't have released
her if she was guilty!

883
01:14:47,090 --> 01:14:49,030
So are you the one who decides that?

884
01:14:49,030 --> 01:14:53,350
Subasi!
You did not do your job properly!

885
01:14:53,860 --> 01:14:56,990
For you, that girl comes first
before your job, Aktemur!

886
01:14:58,990 --> 01:15:00,080
What a shame.

887
01:15:01,010 --> 01:15:01,950
Mother.

888
01:15:03,260 --> 01:15:04,320
Your words are heavy.

889
01:15:04,320 --> 01:15:09,680
Aktemur,
I'll never see you around that girl again.

890
01:15:11,880 --> 01:15:13,200
This is my last warning.

891
01:15:35,440 --> 01:15:39,060
Beautiful, really beautiful fabrics.

892
01:15:40,130 --> 01:15:42,210
These came from Constantinople.

893
01:15:43,390 --> 01:15:46,340
It is as fine as the fabrics
of your clothes.

894
01:15:46,340 --> 01:15:47,500
Don't worry.

895
01:15:48,910 --> 01:15:51,820
Never seen such a dumb flirting.

896
01:15:52,270 --> 01:15:54,500
Have you been to Constantinople before?

897
01:15:55,610 --> 01:15:57,800
Is this a part of our game?

898
01:16:01,870 --> 01:16:03,240
What do you say to him, huh?

899
01:16:05,500 --> 01:16:07,720
I said I grew up in Constantinople.

900
01:16:19,480 --> 01:16:21,150
No, where is he?

901
01:16:23,180 --> 01:16:25,080
He is in Constantinople.

902
01:16:27,090 --> 01:16:28,770
I'm sure of this.

903
01:16:36,220 --> 01:16:38,920
Beautiful, I really like the fabrics.

904
01:16:38,920 --> 01:16:41,380
All my clothes should
be sewn with these fabrics.

905
01:16:46,440 --> 01:16:48,060
What a never ending talk!

906
01:16:48,060 --> 01:16:50,780
It's just a damn fabric.

907
01:16:50,780 --> 01:16:52,870
Like they're preparing for a wedding.

908
01:17:14,010 --> 01:17:14,840
Come on.

909
01:17:22,850 --> 01:17:27,070
When I lost that snake Frig
in the alley, Marta was there too.

910
01:17:27,410 --> 01:17:29,070
I never trust that woman.

911
01:17:29,070 --> 01:17:31,070
The trouble came when Marta came.

912
01:17:33,380 --> 01:17:36,560
Ayse, tell our sisters to keep an eye
on her.

913
01:17:36,680 --> 01:17:38,580
I sent them after her in the morning.

914
01:17:38,590 --> 01:17:42,340
According to our sisters,
Sir Liu is not seen in the market.

915
01:17:43,020 --> 01:17:46,290
We also didn't find that wounded dog
that went to prison that day.

916
01:17:46,290 --> 01:17:47,800
I don't understand.

917
01:17:48,310 --> 01:17:50,070
They are both inside us.

918
01:17:50,220 --> 01:17:51,500
We will find them Malhun.

919
01:17:52,090 --> 01:17:55,880
Once Ulgen arrives, we'll find out
about that Marta.

920
01:17:56,720 --> 01:17:57,880
Inshallah.

921
01:17:58,700 --> 01:18:00,960
Can I come in, Malhun Hatun?

922
01:18:01,280 --> 01:18:02,640
Come in Ulgen.

923
01:18:06,650 --> 01:18:08,920
That infidel Hatun is too picky!

924
01:18:10,100 --> 01:18:13,160
It's just a fabric and they can't decide!
They talk over and over.

925
01:18:13,160 --> 01:18:16,290
What did they talk about?
Do you think they know each other?

926
01:18:17,140 --> 01:18:18,600
I don't know.

927
01:18:18,600 --> 01:18:21,650
They spoke a foreign language,
I didn't understand a single word

928
01:18:21,650 --> 01:18:22,860
Try to remember.

929
01:18:22,880 --> 01:18:25,120
Maybe they told a familiar word?

930
01:18:26,460 --> 01:18:28,950
I heard the word Constantinople.

931
01:18:30,090 --> 01:18:33,340
Other than that,
they just giggled and cackled.

932
01:18:34,690 --> 01:18:38,860
That Marta or whatever is her name,
she set her eyes on that man.

933
01:18:42,100 --> 01:18:44,250
There must be something in this.

934
01:18:45,180 --> 01:18:48,030
We had better follow that Marta.

935
01:18:48,300 --> 01:18:50,030
Let's see what she hides.

936
01:19:06,320 --> 01:19:08,330
It'll fit Kantakuzenos perfectly.

937
01:19:19,830 --> 01:19:21,920
I brought the fabrics you asked, Marta.

938
01:19:47,890 --> 01:19:51,890
Osman, that was the reason
for your absence.

939
01:19:53,700 --> 01:19:57,710
You've healed the emperor but
you are coming back alone.

940
01:20:00,910 --> 01:20:02,620
Get ready.

941
01:20:03,070 --> 01:20:05,620
We will greet Osman Bey.

942
01:20:05,620 --> 01:20:06,890
Yes madam.

943
01:20:17,660 --> 01:20:18,530
Bala Hatun.

944
01:20:21,510 --> 01:20:24,130
There's news from my Bey,
he's approaching.

945
01:20:24,460 --> 01:20:26,900
Good then, prepare you alps, Boran.

946
01:20:26,900 --> 01:20:28,520
I'll come too, we'll go together.

947
01:20:28,520 --> 01:20:29,530
Eyvallah (alright)

948
01:21:07,810 --> 01:21:09,410
Don't be afraid princess, it's me.

949
01:21:09,410 --> 01:21:10,710
Sarkis.

950
01:21:12,570 --> 01:21:15,560
My father...
How is he?

951
01:21:16,100 --> 01:21:18,600
Did you see him? Is he alive?

952
01:21:19,180 --> 01:21:22,470
He's alive, ma'am.
He is conscious.

953
01:21:36,700 --> 01:21:40,390
Jesus the High,
you heard my prayer!

954
01:21:41,340 --> 01:21:42,390
Osman Bey.

955
01:21:44,430 --> 01:21:47,990
His healer saved your father.
They found the antidote.

956
01:21:48,770 --> 01:21:49,990
Osman.

957
01:21:52,410 --> 01:21:54,440
Should I trust him?

958
01:21:54,730 --> 01:21:58,040
Or is this part of the game?
I don't know, Sarkis!

959
01:21:58,300 --> 01:22:00,040
My mind is so confused!

960
01:22:00,540 --> 01:22:02,910
I also have the same doubts, princess.

961
01:22:02,910 --> 01:22:06,120
But Osman Bey saved your father
from death for the second time.

962
01:22:06,120 --> 01:22:08,220
If you consider all the help he lended...

963
01:22:08,940 --> 01:22:10,530
He is still a Turk.

964
01:22:12,030 --> 01:22:14,210
He must have an interest.

965
01:22:14,210 --> 01:22:16,210
You are right, princess.

966
01:22:16,430 --> 01:22:18,880
But there are people
who want to kill you in this city.

967
01:22:19,260 --> 01:22:22,810
Also they think I am a vile reptilian
who wants to kill her father!

968
01:22:23,930 --> 01:22:27,510
They want to kill both me
and my reputation, Sarkis.

969
01:22:27,920 --> 01:22:30,860
You can't stay here
until your innocence is proven.

970
01:22:31,770 --> 01:22:33,970
It seems that going to
Yenişehir is in your best interest.

971
01:22:34,640 --> 01:22:38,380
Those who want to kill me
also want to kill my father, Sarkis.

972
01:22:38,930 --> 01:22:41,530
On top of that,
I don't even know who they are.

973
01:22:41,530 --> 01:22:43,100
How can I leave my father?

974
01:22:44,570 --> 01:22:48,290
There are hundreds of soldiers loyal
to the emperor who can protect him.

975
01:22:49,210 --> 01:22:53,500
But I am afraid that even your father can't
protect you from this slander against you.

976
01:22:54,940 --> 01:22:56,810
What are we going to do now?

977
01:23:24,950 --> 01:23:26,520
Osman Bey!

978
01:23:33,090 --> 01:23:35,580
My Bey! Osman Bey!

979
01:23:39,500 --> 01:23:42,290
Attack.
Kill.

980
01:23:43,640 --> 01:23:44,990
Remove them.

981
01:24:16,050 --> 01:24:17,690
Who are you?

982
01:24:18,210 --> 01:24:21,950
I brought you death.

983
01:24:23,890 --> 01:24:24,920
Osman.

984
01:24:27,470 --> 01:24:29,100
Come to me then.

985
01:24:35,880 --> 01:24:37,140
We are coming my Bey!

986
01:25:01,950 --> 01:25:04,430
Do you always set an ambush to win,
ignoble dog!?

987
01:25:04,680 --> 01:25:09,970
Now I will shed your and Osman's blood.

988
01:25:23,760 --> 01:25:24,860
Cerkutay!

989
01:25:36,230 --> 01:25:38,560
I have an eye behind my head!

990
01:26:28,310 --> 01:26:31,030
No one can save you from me now!

991
01:27:02,300 --> 01:27:04,990
Maybe not today but tomorrow.

992
01:27:20,270 --> 01:27:24,370
Bala, alps!

993
01:27:28,670 --> 01:27:29,440
Bala.

994
01:27:32,110 --> 01:27:32,930
Bala.

995
01:27:35,500 --> 01:27:36,650
You are fine, right?

996
01:27:36,650 --> 01:27:38,240
I'm fine Osman, I'm fine

997
01:27:38,240 --> 01:27:40,620
But I missed that woman who
haunts our children!

998
01:27:40,620 --> 01:27:42,070
No.

999
01:27:45,380 --> 01:27:48,770
We are riding our horses to protect our
children from them.

1000
01:27:49,470 --> 01:27:50,240
Come.

1001
01:27:50,460 --> 01:27:52,580
First our children, then you.

1002
01:27:53,490 --> 01:27:55,400
How many attacks has it been, my Osman?

1003
01:27:56,230 --> 01:27:58,950
But thank Allah you are here safe and sound.

1004
01:27:59,930 --> 01:28:03,020
As long as I have a wife
like you standing behind me...

1005
01:28:03,350 --> 01:28:05,390
...no ambush can hurt us

1006
01:28:05,990 --> 01:28:07,390
Let them attack.

1007
01:28:09,400 --> 01:28:13,920
But their swords do not hurt our heart.

1008
01:28:16,830 --> 01:28:20,080
So tell me, did you see her face?

1009
01:28:20,080 --> 01:28:21,300
No my Bey.

1010
01:28:21,300 --> 01:28:23,700
She clearly doesn't want to be recognized.

1011
01:28:25,210 --> 01:28:27,710
Well, who do you suspect?

1012
01:28:27,710 --> 01:28:29,490
There is one I doubt.

1013
01:28:29,720 --> 01:28:32,470
Let's get to Yenişehir and we'll know.

1014
01:28:34,640 --> 01:28:36,700
Let's go, let's go.

1015
01:28:38,180 --> 01:28:39,270
Let's go, Alps!

1016
01:29:01,950 --> 01:29:05,170
If you allow me, my Bey,
the training is over.

1017
01:29:11,050 --> 01:29:14,250
Brother, take me with you this time.

1018
01:29:14,250 --> 01:29:16,250
I don't have anything to do.

1019
01:29:16,250 --> 01:29:18,250
I'll help you there.

1020
01:29:18,410 --> 01:29:21,110
Your job is to stay here
and take care of your sister.

1021
01:29:21,110 --> 01:29:24,410
But she always sleeps,
I have nothing to do.

1022
01:29:24,920 --> 01:29:28,910
Brother Aladdin, will you also
go with brother Orhan?

1023
01:29:33,310 --> 01:29:34,330
No sister.

1024
01:29:34,330 --> 01:29:39,130
I will go to school in Konya
if Osman Bey permits.

1025
01:29:39,130 --> 01:29:41,680
You're all leaving me!

1026
01:29:41,680 --> 01:29:43,430
Luckily I have a sister.

1027
01:29:48,220 --> 01:29:48,970
Aladdin.

1028
01:29:49,510 --> 01:29:50,510
Face me.

1029
01:29:53,090 --> 01:29:54,400
Come on, raise your sword.

1030
01:30:00,000 --> 01:30:00,710
Let's go.

1031
01:30:16,660 --> 01:30:19,210
Are you running away
to school now, Aladdin?

1032
01:30:19,440 --> 01:30:22,360
Why would you say that, brother?
I am not running away.

1033
01:30:29,880 --> 01:30:31,730
I know your problem
is not with me brother.

1034
01:30:33,080 --> 01:30:35,970
But if you have something to say,
face our father and tell him.

1035
01:30:36,480 --> 01:30:38,840
You can't achieve anything by running away.

1036
01:30:39,140 --> 01:30:40,780
I'm not running away, brother.

1037
01:30:41,030 --> 01:30:44,080
Everyone think I am such a coward and weak.

1038
01:30:44,080 --> 01:30:46,760
So they consider everything
I do is running away.

1039
01:30:50,780 --> 01:30:51,780
Excuse me, brother.

1040
01:30:52,710 --> 01:30:54,260
I have to go to school now.

1041
01:31:05,320 --> 01:31:06,480
Life is hard, brother.

1042
01:31:07,670 --> 01:31:08,890
And you will learn, too.

1043
01:31:09,780 --> 01:31:12,470
You will grow up and mature anyway.

1044
01:31:14,240 --> 01:31:15,610
My brave brother.

1045
01:31:16,480 --> 01:31:19,500
We can face the whole world together,
with the heart of yours!

1046
01:31:22,930 --> 01:31:24,110
Can I come in, my Bey?

1047
01:31:29,080 --> 01:31:30,320
Are you alone, Huseyin?

1048
01:31:30,320 --> 01:31:31,300
Yes my Bey!

1049
01:31:32,000 --> 01:31:33,000
Come.

1050
01:31:47,110 --> 01:31:48,580
Did you figure it out?

1051
01:31:48,690 --> 01:31:51,480
What happened to the gold?
Where did all this gold go?

1052
01:31:53,110 --> 01:31:55,480
Didn't he make a pact with the emperor?

1053
01:31:56,230 --> 01:31:59,950
It is clear that the gold
goes to Constantinople.

1054
01:32:02,070 --> 01:32:03,910
There was a lot of gold.

1055
01:32:06,010 --> 01:32:11,150
Considering that the heads of this plan
sacrifice so much gold...

1056
01:32:12,570 --> 01:32:13,820
...maybe...

1057
01:32:14,340 --> 01:32:17,940
...we can find more than this
if we keep tracking.

1058
01:32:21,230 --> 01:32:23,330
You didn't understand, did you, Huseyin?

1059
01:32:23,750 --> 01:32:27,150
- I didn't understand, my Bey.
- You'll understand, you'll understand.

1060
01:32:29,200 --> 01:32:30,200
What I mean is...

1061
01:32:32,660 --> 01:32:36,040
...in which scenario do I earn more?
Should I sell Olof to Osman...

1062
01:32:37,040 --> 01:32:39,540
Or should I sell Osman to Olof?

1063
01:32:40,940 --> 01:32:43,130
Our Oktam Bey will be fine but...

1064
01:32:45,400 --> 01:32:47,180
...we should think it through.

1065
01:32:56,620 --> 01:33:00,010
Check carefully throughout the tribe.

1066
01:33:01,220 --> 01:33:04,750
Who knows, maybe there's
more gold somewhere else.

1067
01:33:05,890 --> 01:33:06,980
As you order, my Bey!

1068
01:33:27,760 --> 01:33:33,250
Welcome, Osman Bey.

1069
01:33:33,500 --> 01:33:35,520
Welcome, Osman Bey.

1070
01:33:53,780 --> 01:33:55,270
Here you go, Osman Bey.

1071
01:33:57,080 --> 01:33:58,730
Host your infidel guest the best!

1072
01:33:59,990 --> 01:34:02,100
Make sure your guest feels comfortable.

1073
01:34:02,370 --> 01:34:05,840
However, I will not let you
have my Bey.

1074
01:34:07,540 --> 01:34:10,110
Let's hope that Osman Bey realizes
his mistake.

1075
01:34:11,640 --> 01:34:13,680
Otherwise, there will be a bloodshed.

1076
01:34:13,770 --> 01:34:17,060
Their justice is
in favor of the infidels, my daughter.

1077
01:34:17,650 --> 01:34:19,370
Come on, don't waste your time.

1078
01:34:20,050 --> 01:34:21,930
Take a good look around.

1079
01:34:23,260 --> 01:34:25,790
Did that Kantakuzenos dog
get out of the mansion?

1080
01:34:26,130 --> 01:34:28,980
- No, he's not out yet. He's still in.
- Good.

1081
01:34:30,080 --> 01:34:31,760
Go and check around.

1082
01:34:33,420 --> 01:34:36,000
And when that dog comes out,
we'll take him down.

1083
01:34:37,290 --> 01:34:40,420
Your father's innocence is up to him.

1084
01:34:52,900 --> 01:34:55,060
Sisters, go straight to Marta's shop.

1085
01:35:00,490 --> 01:35:01,490
Alcicek.

1086
01:35:06,280 --> 01:35:07,550
Alcicek Hatun.

1087
01:35:09,430 --> 01:35:10,670
What are you doing here?

1088
01:35:10,890 --> 01:35:12,450
Don't you have another job?

1089
01:35:14,380 --> 01:35:15,700
Are you watching me?

1090
01:35:16,780 --> 01:35:17,780
Well...

1091
01:35:18,000 --> 01:35:20,150
It's hard to tell what's your next move is.

1092
01:35:20,150 --> 01:35:21,680
I wanted to warn you beforehand.

1093
01:35:22,740 --> 01:35:25,030
- Why did you come?
- What do you think?

1094
01:35:25,820 --> 01:35:27,850
What are my people going to eat, Subasi?

1095
01:35:28,030 --> 01:35:30,020
I am managing our stall in the market.

1096
01:35:32,130 --> 01:35:33,130
Alps!

1097
01:35:36,520 --> 01:35:38,780
Please escort Alcicek Hatun
to her stall.

1098
01:35:41,070 --> 01:35:42,530
Keep your eyes on her.

1099
01:35:43,110 --> 01:35:44,830
There is no need for this, Subasi.

1100
01:35:45,200 --> 01:35:46,200
Hatun.

1101
01:35:47,880 --> 01:35:49,460
Either alps accompany you...

1102
01:35:50,560 --> 01:35:52,250
...or you will return to your tent.

1103
01:35:53,130 --> 01:35:54,130
Alcicek!

1104
01:36:03,840 --> 01:36:05,530
You turned our tribe into a prison.

1105
01:36:06,360 --> 01:36:09,440
Now, are you going to make
Yenisehir a prison for us, Subasi?

1106
01:36:16,430 --> 01:36:17,430
Come on

1107
01:36:17,980 --> 01:36:18,980
Go to the stall.

1108
01:36:30,320 --> 01:36:31,320
Subasi.

1109
01:36:32,440 --> 01:36:36,210
Keep your eyes off my daughter, Subasi.

1110
01:36:38,380 --> 01:36:40,220
Otherwise, I will gouge your eyes out.

1111
01:36:43,450 --> 01:36:45,460
What are you talking about, Bengi Hatun?

1112
01:36:48,100 --> 01:36:49,100
I am...

1113
01:37:24,580 --> 01:37:27,190
If we take in a bit more,
it will fit perfectly.

1114
01:37:27,810 --> 01:37:30,720
How long will this woman stay here?

1115
01:37:32,640 --> 01:37:34,750
I'll find a way to get her out of here.

1116
01:37:35,430 --> 01:37:38,360
I can do this another way too.

1117
01:37:46,920 --> 01:37:47,920
Speak our language.

1118
01:37:49,290 --> 01:37:51,200
Or do your job without talking.

1119
01:38:01,900 --> 01:38:03,030
Where is your wound?

1120
01:38:09,560 --> 01:38:11,150
Either the shooter is not skilled

1121
01:38:11,900 --> 01:38:13,600
...or he didn't want to kill you.

1122
01:38:15,340 --> 01:38:17,480
A fly bite does not kill a lion.

1123
01:38:17,690 --> 01:38:18,980
That wound is unimportant.

1124
01:38:18,980 --> 01:38:20,520
Where have you been, Osman Bey?

1125
01:38:28,010 --> 01:38:29,840
Did you have these clothes stitch?

1126
01:38:32,820 --> 01:38:33,910
Yes.

1127
01:38:34,860 --> 01:38:36,370
Tailored by our best tailors.

1128
01:38:41,440 --> 01:38:42,670
Get this Hatun out of the mansion.

1129
01:38:57,530 --> 01:38:58,900
I come from Constantinople.

1130
01:39:00,570 --> 01:39:01,660
Why?

1131
01:39:02,220 --> 01:39:03,700
They poisoned the emperor.

1132
01:39:06,990 --> 01:39:08,890
Don't worry, he's fine.

1133
01:39:10,790 --> 01:39:14,410
You showed me the darkness first, then you
showed me the light, Osman Bey.

1134
01:39:15,150 --> 01:39:17,720
There is a lot of information
I have to tell you.

1135
01:39:17,720 --> 01:39:19,530
But they're not good news.

1136
01:39:20,680 --> 01:39:22,790
-What does that mean?
-Can I come in, my Bey?

1137
01:39:24,560 --> 01:39:25,670
Come.

1138
01:39:27,500 --> 01:39:29,170
My Bey, Dursun has come.

1139
01:39:31,270 --> 01:39:33,260
Let's solve Oktem Bey issue first.

1140
01:39:35,970 --> 01:39:37,370
Let's go to the court.

1141
01:39:48,020 --> 01:39:49,030
Marta.

1142
01:39:51,470 --> 01:39:52,940
Prince Kantakuzenos.

1143
01:39:53,770 --> 01:39:55,360
I hope he likes his dress.

1144
01:39:55,900 --> 01:39:56,990
Yes, yes.

1145
01:39:57,690 --> 01:39:58,710
He was very grateful.

1146
01:39:59,120 --> 01:40:01,490
It is very important to
make the guest happy.

1147
01:40:04,880 --> 01:40:06,010
Marta!

1148
01:40:17,650 --> 01:40:19,420
I was looking for you in the sky.

1149
01:40:19,530 --> 01:40:20,880
I found you on earth.

1150
01:40:24,450 --> 01:40:25,520
I am here

1151
01:40:26,230 --> 01:40:27,240
Bala Hatun.

1152
01:40:27,830 --> 01:40:29,490
I am coming from the market.

1153
01:40:29,960 --> 01:40:31,220
I stopped by the shop, but...

1154
01:40:32,100 --> 01:40:34,560
I couldn't see both you and Leo.

1155
01:40:35,790 --> 01:40:36,870
So you were here.

1156
01:40:38,770 --> 01:40:42,210
Sometimes you just can't see them
even if they're just in front of you.

1157
01:40:43,680 --> 01:40:46,620
My brother Leo went to
Constantinople to get fabric.

1158
01:40:47,380 --> 01:40:49,730
And I'm here for the prince.

1159
01:40:56,250 --> 01:40:57,310
So...

1160
01:40:58,460 --> 01:40:59,690
Why were you looking for me?

1161
01:41:02,300 --> 01:41:03,360
For fabric.

1162
01:41:08,190 --> 01:41:09,200
Marta.

1163
01:41:14,920 --> 01:41:16,340
I wanted to see the new fabrics.

1164
01:41:22,180 --> 01:41:23,820
What you are wearing is...

1165
01:41:24,060 --> 01:41:25,400
...very eye-catching.

1166
01:41:27,240 --> 01:41:28,700
You deserve better.

1167
01:41:29,520 --> 01:41:31,350
But I have a lot of these fabrics.

1168
01:41:32,020 --> 01:41:34,520
When you stop by, I'll show you,
Bala Hatun.

1169
01:41:40,710 --> 01:41:41,970
Excuse me now.

1170
01:41:43,340 --> 01:41:44,430
Of course.

1171
01:41:45,150 --> 01:41:46,570
I will visit you someday.

1172
01:41:47,340 --> 01:41:48,410
Anytime you want.

1173
01:41:49,140 --> 01:41:50,490
But I'm not available today.

1174
01:41:52,500 --> 01:41:54,170
I will hand over the fabrics.

1175
01:42:07,140 --> 01:42:08,240
What happened, Bala?

1176
01:42:11,430 --> 01:42:13,920
We got very close to that snake Frig,
Malhun Hatun.

1177
01:42:13,920 --> 01:42:14,920
Very close.

1178
01:42:15,480 --> 01:42:16,550
Are you okay?

1179
01:42:16,680 --> 01:42:18,020
What happened to your hand?

1180
01:42:18,020 --> 01:42:19,520
I'm fine fine, I'll tell you.

1181
01:42:20,210 --> 01:42:22,300
Ayse, inform Aktemur.

1182
01:42:23,190 --> 01:42:25,410
- We'll follow her.
- Alright.

1183
01:42:26,830 --> 01:42:28,760
Let's see what she is hiding.

1184
01:42:30,830 --> 01:42:32,180
Let's go to the healer first...

1185
01:42:46,410 --> 01:42:48,250
Hurry up, I'm in a hurry

1186
01:43:05,900 --> 01:43:07,940
Let's see if you're
clear or dirty, Marta.

1187
01:43:08,740 --> 01:43:10,790
Ayse, take care of it here.

1188
01:43:11,640 --> 01:43:13,110
Aktemur, let's go.

1189
01:43:18,410 --> 01:43:19,510
Alcicek!

1190
01:43:20,130 --> 01:43:22,150
- Here.
- Ayse Hatun?

1191
01:43:25,410 --> 01:43:26,790
I have heard about you.

1192
01:43:27,940 --> 01:43:29,550
Aktemur pitied you.

1193
01:43:30,720 --> 01:43:31,870
And he didn't say anything to you

1194
01:43:33,180 --> 01:43:34,900
But I am not like Aktemur.

1195
01:43:37,380 --> 01:43:38,590
I have no mercy.

1196
01:43:40,850 --> 01:43:41,870
Did he pity me?

1197
01:43:42,980 --> 01:43:44,090
Did he?

1198
01:43:45,460 --> 01:43:46,470
Let him know.

1199
01:43:47,290 --> 01:43:48,700
He should never pity us.

1200
01:43:49,700 --> 01:43:51,400
Tell him, I won't pity him either.

1201
01:43:54,550 --> 01:43:56,870
You will be punished for your actions.

1202
01:43:57,950 --> 01:44:00,850
You will answer to Osman Bey, Alcicek.

1203
01:44:01,340 --> 01:44:03,590
I haven't done anything I can't answer.

1204
01:44:04,690 --> 01:44:07,040
I am here, responsible for all my acitons.

1205
01:44:08,200 --> 01:44:09,540
Now get out of my way.

1206
01:44:14,390 --> 01:44:16,130
You can definitely answer.

1207
01:44:18,260 --> 01:44:22,320
But you can't pay for what you did
to my son.

1208
01:44:23,200 --> 01:44:27,000
I don't want to see
you around my son again.

1209
01:44:30,430 --> 01:44:31,480
Go now.

1210
01:44:35,780 --> 01:44:37,780
Pity, huh? Subasi!

1211
01:44:39,600 --> 01:44:42,210
You will cause trouble for my son.

1212
01:44:43,700 --> 01:44:45,280
But I won't allow you.

1213
01:45:00,410 --> 01:45:01,490
Here.

1214
01:45:10,340 --> 01:45:11,360
Kantakuzenos...

1215
01:45:12,170 --> 01:45:14,650
...wants Oktem Bey to pay.

1216
01:45:17,750 --> 01:45:19,140
With the court...

1217
01:45:19,630 --> 01:45:22,450
...we'll reveal the truth
one way or another.

1218
01:45:23,360 --> 01:45:26,580
Since the guilt is so clear,
the court makes no sense.

1219
01:45:27,080 --> 01:45:28,320
Oktem Bey is guilty.

1220
01:45:32,130 --> 01:45:34,100
The reason for court to take place...

1221
01:45:35,620 --> 01:45:37,500
...is to show the truth in public.

1222
01:45:40,450 --> 01:45:44,470
The evidence proves Oktem Bey guilty.

1223
01:45:48,150 --> 01:45:49,170
However...

1224
01:45:51,700 --> 01:45:53,990
There is no judgment to be decided now.

1225
01:45:54,870 --> 01:45:56,200
Let the court reveal...

1226
01:45:56,850 --> 01:45:59,590
...who is guilty and who is not.

1227
01:46:03,610 --> 01:46:04,660
Boran!

1228
01:46:05,570 --> 01:46:06,760
Come here.

1229
01:46:18,570 --> 01:46:22,950
How can you make him face me?
His hands are not even tied!

1230
01:46:24,020 --> 01:46:26,670
Kantakuzenos.

1231
01:46:31,200 --> 01:46:32,430
Oktem Bey.

1232
01:46:35,955 --> 01:46:37,975
Why do you disobey?

1233
01:46:38,350 --> 01:46:42,250
For the same reason why you disobeyed
the Sultan and the Vizier.

1234
01:46:44,550 --> 01:46:45,820
I disobey for the right.

1235
01:46:45,820 --> 01:46:47,820
And for the sake of justice, Osman Bey.

1236
01:46:48,300 --> 01:46:52,050
I was considered a disobedient
because I did not trust their justice.

1237
01:46:54,700 --> 01:46:57,150
Why don't you trust my justice?

1238
01:46:57,850 --> 01:46:59,720
You oppose Turgut Bey.

1239
01:47:00,670 --> 01:47:03,320
You raise your sword to Kantakuzenos.

1240
01:47:05,700 --> 01:47:08,020
These are already a crime.

1241
01:47:08,950 --> 01:47:11,270
What's more, you are involved in
the gold issue.

1242
01:47:12,250 --> 01:47:13,550
That's a slander.

1243
01:47:15,300 --> 01:47:20,820
If it is true and not slander, I will cut
your head and hang it in your tribe.

1244
01:47:22,170 --> 01:47:23,600
Eyvallah (okay).

1245
01:47:26,750 --> 01:47:29,150
Dursun Fakih will judge you.

1246
01:47:31,370 --> 01:47:39,180
If this court won't cut Oktem Bey's head,
then there's no need for it, Osman Bey.

1247
01:47:40,170 --> 01:47:43,400
Whether the evidence proves
Oktem Bey guilty or not...

1248
01:47:44,420 --> 01:47:47,770
Neither you nor I can be sure about that.

1249
01:47:48,800 --> 01:47:50,850
Only the court will decide that.

1250
01:47:50,850 --> 01:47:53,370
Then I will secure my own justice.

1251
01:47:54,700 --> 01:47:57,240
I will come with a great
army from Constantinople...

1252
01:47:57,240 --> 01:47:59,120
...and the agreement will be over.

1253
01:47:59,770 --> 01:48:04,150
Neither you can end the agreement
nor you can come with a great army.

1254
01:48:05,600 --> 01:48:07,080
What do you mean?

1255
01:48:07,670 --> 01:48:10,350
Are you testing my power, Osman Bey?

1256
01:48:13,250 --> 01:48:14,820
Stay patient.

1257
01:48:15,350 --> 01:48:16,970
We'll hear everything.

1258
01:48:21,650 --> 01:48:23,400
Everyone, go out.

1259
01:48:25,600 --> 01:48:27,520
Except for Kantakuzenos.

1260
01:49:19,370 --> 01:49:21,000
We are being followed.

1261
01:49:22,120 --> 01:49:23,350
Let me see.

1262
01:49:24,250 --> 01:49:25,870
Be careful.

1263
01:49:47,800 --> 01:49:50,870
Come on, keep your eyes open.

1264
01:49:56,370 --> 01:50:00,570
I will learn whom you are after and
what you are up to. I'll know everything.

1265
01:50:16,870 --> 01:50:18,170
Tell me, Osman Bey.

1266
01:50:18,450 --> 01:50:19,970
I want to know everything.

1267
01:50:20,470 --> 01:50:23,420
The emperor does not trust you.

1268
01:50:26,700 --> 01:50:29,570
Felic, Ophelia and you...

1269
01:50:31,120 --> 01:50:33,400
He thinks you have ambitions for the throne.

1270
01:50:33,400 --> 01:50:34,120
What?

1271
01:50:36,070 --> 01:50:37,400
Stupid man.

1272
01:50:38,120 --> 01:50:40,420
Stupid man.

1273
01:50:40,970 --> 01:50:43,100
What caused this thought of his...

1274
01:50:45,520 --> 01:50:47,920
...while I covered his back.

1275
01:50:47,920 --> 01:50:49,350
Did you cause this thought?

1276
01:50:49,350 --> 01:50:51,200
Can it be because of your acts?

1277
01:50:53,300 --> 01:50:55,900
Olof was with me in Constantinople.

1278
01:50:57,820 --> 01:50:59,050
Did you send him?

1279
01:50:59,050 --> 01:51:01,050
Yes, I sent him.

1280
01:51:01,700 --> 01:51:04,370
To catch the traitor named Ophelia.

1281
01:51:04,370 --> 01:51:06,370
And now he's chasing you.

1282
01:51:07,120 --> 01:51:10,720
He will kill you at the first opportunity
he gets, by order of the Emperor.

1283
01:51:11,520 --> 01:51:12,820
No.

1284
01:51:13,600 --> 01:51:15,770
No, something like this can't happen.

1285
01:51:17,120 --> 01:51:19,900
Even if the emperor gave such an order...

1286
01:51:19,900 --> 01:51:21,900
Olof is loyal to me.

1287
01:51:22,220 --> 01:51:23,900
He won't do such thing.

1288
01:51:25,670 --> 01:51:28,570
Well, I warned you.

1289
01:51:30,750 --> 01:51:32,150
Take precautions if you want.

1290
01:51:37,750 --> 01:51:39,620
Are your soldiers enough?

1291
01:51:43,250 --> 01:51:45,300
Olof will kill me, huh?

1292
01:51:45,300 --> 01:51:47,300
If you side with me, I will protect you.

1293
01:51:51,250 --> 01:51:53,900
Will the Prince of Rome seek help
from a Turk?

1294
01:51:58,950 --> 01:52:00,000
Go then.

1295
01:52:00,970 --> 01:52:03,550
When you leave the borders of Yenişehir...

1296
01:52:03,850 --> 01:52:06,050
...your executioners
will be waiting for you.

1297
01:52:14,600 --> 01:52:16,770
What do we do then?

1298
01:52:30,970 --> 01:52:32,070
Boran.

1299
01:52:32,450 --> 01:52:33,500
My Bey.

1300
01:52:34,300 --> 01:52:36,450
Take dear Prince to
the secret place.

1301
01:52:38,220 --> 01:52:40,220
He's under our protection.

1302
01:52:43,200 --> 01:52:46,150
As you order, my Bey.

1303
01:54:28,920 --> 01:54:30,700
Oh Alcicek!

1304
01:54:31,070 --> 01:54:33,400
How could you do that to a young boy.

1305
01:55:12,000 --> 01:55:13,420
Is he still not able to hear?

1306
01:55:14,570 --> 01:55:16,200
Yes my Bey!

1307
01:55:19,900 --> 01:55:22,270
He doesn't hear, my Bey.

1308
01:55:23,870 --> 01:55:26,550
But he acts like he hears!

1309
01:55:27,570 --> 01:55:29,200
When will he hear?

1310
01:55:29,200 --> 01:55:31,200
It will take some time, my Bey.

1311
01:55:31,200 --> 01:55:33,200
But he will hear again.

1312
01:55:34,220 --> 01:55:36,520
He has to track.

1313
01:55:37,650 --> 01:55:40,220
You'll take care of it, Kumral Abdal.

1314
01:55:45,070 --> 01:55:47,370
I can track my Bey!
Who do you want me to find?

1315
01:55:53,320 --> 01:55:55,100
Tracing is done, Cerkutay.

1316
01:55:55,750 --> 01:55:57,400
We need your sword now.

1317
01:56:00,420 --> 01:56:01,650
Kumral Abdal.

1318
01:56:02,850 --> 01:56:04,520
Tell me where Olof is.

1319
01:56:07,150 --> 01:56:09,120
He lives near Macri, my Bey.

1320
01:56:10,600 --> 01:56:12,050
On the rocky beach.

1321
01:56:14,400 --> 01:56:17,220
Their place is secured.
They are crowded.

1322
01:56:35,970 --> 01:56:38,900
You are doing your job properly,
Kumral Abdal.

1323
01:56:39,950 --> 01:56:41,920
Now the enemy is clear.

1324
01:56:41,920 --> 01:56:43,920
You know what to do.

1325
01:56:45,000 --> 01:56:46,900
Now listen to me very carefully.

1326
01:56:57,720 --> 01:56:59,200
Stop!

1327
01:57:00,190 --> 01:57:02,100
I told you to stop!

1328
01:57:24,000 --> 01:57:25,350
Marta.

1329
01:57:26,810 --> 01:57:28,330
Bala Hatun?

1330
01:57:28,970 --> 01:57:30,520
What's going on?

1331
01:57:30,880 --> 01:57:32,790
Check her, alps!

1332
01:58:10,120 --> 01:58:11,950
Bala Hatun.

1333
01:58:12,130 --> 01:58:14,120
Why don't you say something?

1334
01:58:14,450 --> 01:58:16,330
Did we make a mistake?

1335
01:58:16,540 --> 01:58:18,860
We only carry fabrics.

1336
01:58:19,030 --> 01:58:20,690
Don't mind me, Marta.

1337
01:58:20,890 --> 01:58:24,130
Inspection is required as a precaution.

1338
01:58:27,030 --> 01:58:30,420
Here comes the fabric merchant.

1339
01:58:34,980 --> 01:58:36,550
Oh my great God!

1340
01:58:37,040 --> 01:58:39,560
You scared me so much, Bala Hatun.

1341
01:58:39,810 --> 01:58:42,110
There is nothing to be scared of, Marta.

1342
01:58:43,230 --> 01:58:46,410
Bala Hatun!
We need you!

1343
01:58:46,590 --> 01:58:48,520
It's Aktemur Bey!

1344
01:58:48,800 --> 01:58:51,040
Let's go alps!

1345
01:58:55,420 --> 01:59:00,080
How sadly, how upsetting.

1346
01:59:02,780 --> 01:59:06,170
They shot Aktemur Bey, Bala Hatun!

1347
01:59:07,260 --> 01:59:10,190
Son!
Alps, get in the position!

1348
01:59:10,320 --> 01:59:14,320
Aktemur, son!
Open your eyes, son!

1349
01:59:20,390 --> 01:59:23,710
Son, are you okay, son?

1350
01:59:26,630 --> 01:59:30,830
Aktemur, hold on, son!
Hold on!

1351
01:59:50,300 --> 01:59:52,310
This bow...

1352
01:59:56,790 --> 01:59:59,980
My Allah! They trapped me!

1353
02:00:08,120 --> 02:00:11,220
Bala Hatun!
The shooter of Aktemur is here!

1354
02:00:16,090 --> 02:00:17,500
Move!

1355
02:00:19,750 --> 02:00:21,130
Move!

1356
02:00:23,050 --> 02:00:26,670
- What have you done, Alcicek!
- Bala Hatun.

1357
02:00:27,010 --> 02:00:29,100
- I was...
- Shut up

1358
02:00:36,150 --> 02:00:38,130
Aktemur.

1359
02:00:40,830 --> 02:00:42,710
Aktemur.

1360
02:00:43,380 --> 02:00:45,440
I didn't do this.

1361
02:00:46,060 --> 02:00:48,550
- I was ne...
- I told you to shut up!

1362
02:00:48,730 --> 02:00:51,490
Let's go to Yenişehir quickly,
he's seriously injured!

1363
02:00:52,720 --> 02:00:54,950
Imprison Alcicek.

1364
02:00:55,110 --> 02:00:57,010
I did not do this!

1365
02:01:17,760 --> 02:01:19,770
My love!

1366
02:01:22,260 --> 02:01:26,870
We didn't succeed, we didn't!
We didn't succeed this time either!

1367
02:01:27,190 --> 02:01:30,430
Osman is alive.

1368
02:01:30,990 --> 02:01:36,990
Your anger, your anger is
what binds me to you.

1369
02:01:37,290 --> 02:01:39,210
Don't worry.

1370
02:01:39,620 --> 02:01:41,970
I will remove Osman.

1371
02:01:42,560 --> 02:01:47,110
I came with an army from Constantinople.

1372
02:01:47,410 --> 02:01:49,600
Osman will die.

1373
02:01:50,490 --> 02:01:53,760
I've never smelt death like this.

1374
02:01:54,000 --> 02:01:55,120
Tell me.

1375
02:01:55,360 --> 02:01:57,370
Oktem's trial...

1376
02:01:57,580 --> 02:02:00,400
...will carry our black curse to Yenişehir

1377
02:02:00,660 --> 02:02:06,130
And Yenişehir will get to meet Frig.

1378
02:02:15,730 --> 02:02:17,760
Oh my love.

1379
02:02:20,730 --> 02:02:24,240
Painting my face and
hugging you on the battlefield...

1380
02:02:25,170 --> 02:02:30,250
I've been waiting for this war
for a long time.

1381
02:02:30,460 --> 02:02:32,230
No.

1382
02:02:33,940 --> 02:02:35,720
No.

1383
02:02:36,680 --> 02:02:39,150
This is not a war.

1384
02:02:39,320 --> 02:02:42,470
This will be our slaughter.

1385
02:02:45,330 --> 02:02:49,320
mumbling

1386
02:03:05,810 --> 02:03:07,980
Come in, hurry up!

1387
02:03:08,240 --> 02:03:10,430
Don't scream!
He'll hear!

1388
02:03:10,670 --> 02:03:13,290
He has become deaf,
he will not hear us, my daughter.

1389
02:03:13,430 --> 02:03:16,190
Hurry up, let's put the blanket on
before he wakes up

1390
02:03:17,380 --> 02:03:20,140
He surely has an eye behind his head.

1391
02:03:33,280 --> 02:03:35,150
Take it, daughter.

1392
02:03:38,300 --> 02:03:41,620
Evil eyes shall stay away!

1393
02:03:41,830 --> 02:03:44,680
The ones with evil eye shall crack!

1394
02:03:44,820 --> 02:03:48,190
Enviers shall suffer!
Their ears shall break!

1395
02:03:48,610 --> 02:03:50,670
Against the evil eyes!

1396
02:03:50,790 --> 02:03:51,860
Get out now!

1397
02:04:03,670 --> 02:04:06,080
There is an evil eye!
There is an evil eye!

1398
02:04:14,800 --> 02:04:16,970
Cerkutay.

1399
02:04:17,230 --> 02:04:19,800
Cerkutay wouldn't die!

1400
02:04:21,320 --> 02:04:24,540
I was immortal?!

1401
02:04:27,260 --> 02:04:29,270
Did I die???

1402
02:04:30,480 --> 02:04:32,960
I guess I died in the war.

1403
02:04:36,400 --> 02:04:39,130
No.
The war hasn't started yet.

1404
02:04:39,410 --> 02:04:41,700
I didn't go to the war.

1405
02:04:44,040 --> 02:04:47,430
Oh so this is a dream.

1406
02:04:49,770 --> 02:04:51,550
My plate is empty.

1407
02:04:52,160 --> 02:04:53,820
There's no food.

1408
02:04:54,490 --> 02:04:56,640
I don't have a dream where
I don't eat.

1409
02:04:56,990 --> 02:05:01,040
They must have poisoned me.

1410
02:05:02,210 --> 02:05:05,570
That woman Ulgen Hatun
must have poisoned me!

1411
02:05:10,720 --> 02:05:13,230
Do you mean me, Cerkutay?

1412
02:05:21,730 --> 02:05:23,270
A nightmare!

1413
02:05:50,840 --> 02:05:55,490
No, no, no, it's a nightmare!
A nightmare!

1414
02:05:55,630 --> 02:05:58,870
Just go back to sleep.
Go back to sleep now.

1415
02:06:00,770 --> 02:06:03,060
Do we know the shooter of Kantakuzenos?

1416
02:06:03,230 --> 02:06:08,180
Someone is playing a game here,
but we will know soon.

1417
02:06:08,420 --> 02:06:10,570
We will know it all.

1418
02:06:11,130 --> 02:06:14,140
Kantakuzenos is under my control.

1419
02:06:14,450 --> 02:06:16,650
Olof's place is also known.

1420
02:06:16,930 --> 02:06:18,560
There is also Oktem Bey.

1421
02:06:19,030 --> 02:06:24,020
I am sure about his innocence,
but we need a proof.

1422
02:06:24,640 --> 02:06:26,000
Yes.

1423
02:06:26,250 --> 02:06:30,790
They grit their teeth
and we grit our teeth

1424
02:06:31,070 --> 02:06:34,720
But when the dog shows his tooth...

1425
02:06:35,040 --> 02:06:37,620
We'll bite that dog on the neck.

1426
02:06:39,000 --> 02:06:41,500
Now that we know
where that dog Olof is...

1427
02:06:41,660 --> 02:06:44,030
...we must kill him after
what he has done to us.

1428
02:06:44,030 --> 02:06:46,150
The emperor sent Olof.

1429
02:06:46,380 --> 02:06:49,960
We will not kill Olof and go against
the Emperor now.

1430
02:06:51,320 --> 02:06:54,540
Even the emperor does business
behind our back.

1431
02:06:54,750 --> 02:06:57,140
He thinks we don't realize.

1432
02:06:57,720 --> 02:07:00,080
Let them setup the game.

1433
02:07:00,640 --> 02:07:03,430
But we will rule them.

1434
02:07:07,450 --> 02:07:09,430
My Allah!

1435
02:07:10,980 --> 02:07:17,060
Slander is a very deep well.

1436
02:07:17,760 --> 02:07:21,170
A very dark well it is.

1437
02:07:21,520 --> 02:07:25,330
There is no evidence of my innocence
on the earth.

1438
02:07:26,150 --> 02:07:32,600
Your Messenger, with his beautiful face,
had a torn shirt, at least.

1439
02:07:34,720 --> 02:07:37,510
But I am facing this slander...

1440
02:07:38,270 --> 02:07:41,060
...all helpless, all naked, my Creator.

1441
02:07:42,390 --> 02:07:47,500
My Allah, I have no one else
to seek help but You.

1442
02:07:48,120 --> 02:07:50,010
You know what's the secret.

1443
02:07:50,580 --> 02:07:52,710
And you light up the darkness.

1444
02:07:53,910 --> 02:07:56,270
Save me from this well, my Creator.

1445
02:07:57,020 --> 02:07:58,350
Amen.

1446
02:08:05,210 --> 02:08:07,500
Leave me, leave me!

1447
02:08:07,760 --> 02:08:08,870
leave me!

1448
02:08:08,870 --> 02:08:10,620
I told you to leave me, leave me!

1449
02:08:10,620 --> 02:08:11,480
Alcicek.

1450
02:08:11,480 --> 02:08:12,720
leave me!

1451
02:08:13,640 --> 02:08:14,830
Father.

1452
02:08:20,020 --> 02:08:21,350
What is this about?

1453
02:08:21,430 --> 02:08:23,280
What are you doing here, Alcicek?

1454
02:08:24,040 --> 02:08:26,060
They played a big game, father.

1455
02:08:26,520 --> 02:08:28,480
They wounded Subasi
and blamed me.

1456
02:08:29,290 --> 02:08:30,810
That's enough!

1457
02:08:32,500 --> 02:08:35,330
This is enough already!

1458
02:08:36,730 --> 02:08:38,870
I will not let them get away with this.

1459
02:08:39,360 --> 02:08:40,800
I won't, daughter.

1460
02:08:46,200 --> 02:08:48,540
Bring a piece of cloth and
hot water quickly!

1461
02:08:48,540 --> 02:08:50,580
Come on, hold on, my valiant!

1462
02:08:51,180 --> 02:08:52,500
Hold on Aktemur.

1463
02:08:56,290 --> 02:08:58,860
Aktemur! Aktemur!

1464
02:08:59,270 --> 02:09:01,560
Aktemur! Aktemur!

1465
02:09:01,560 --> 02:09:02,660
What happened?

1466
02:09:03,190 --> 02:09:05,450
What happened Bala?

1467
02:09:05,450 --> 02:09:07,900
What happened? Who did this?

1468
02:09:07,900 --> 02:09:09,510
Ayse, I'll tell you.

1469
02:09:09,510 --> 02:09:11,880
He was hit by two arrows, the wounds
are critical.

1470
02:09:11,880 --> 02:09:14,990
Let's take off his clothes,
let's take off his clothes

1471
02:09:15,625 --> 02:09:16,625
Son!

1472
02:09:16,700 --> 02:09:18,280
Wait, Aktemur!

1473
02:09:18,280 --> 02:09:19,950
Aktemur!

1474
02:09:20,460 --> 02:09:22,760
Give me the cloth!

1475
02:09:32,220 --> 02:09:33,560
Aktemur!

1476
02:09:34,340 --> 02:09:35,560
Who did this?

1477
02:09:41,120 --> 02:09:42,620
The daughter of Oktem Bey.

1478
02:09:42,620 --> 02:09:44,950
- Alcicek.
- What?

1479
02:09:46,350 --> 02:09:47,940
This is unbelievable!

1480
02:09:48,620 --> 02:09:51,300
She wouldn't!
Why would she do that?

1481
02:09:58,400 --> 02:09:59,720
That snake!

1482
02:10:00,930 --> 02:10:03,660
That snake!
That snake!

1483
02:10:04,050 --> 02:10:07,500
I knew she would do something.

1484
02:10:08,070 --> 02:10:09,850
I told you to stay away from her!

1485
02:10:09,990 --> 02:10:12,170
You didn't listen to me, Aktemur!

1486
02:10:12,170 --> 02:10:14,030
I told you to stay away from her!

1487
02:10:15,780 --> 02:10:16,750
Hold on!

1488
02:10:17,050 --> 02:10:18,670
Hold on, dear, I'm here!

1489
02:10:19,360 --> 02:10:22,320
Aktemur!
We must take them out.

1490
02:10:23,780 --> 02:10:25,150
We should take them out.

1491
02:10:29,570 --> 02:10:31,140
So, Osman Bey...

1492
02:10:31,640 --> 02:10:33,990
...one more time,
we are alone wolves again.

1493
02:10:34,090 --> 02:10:36,740
The one who is in a difficult situation
has few friends.

1494
02:10:37,010 --> 02:10:39,930
Who said we will be crowded
when we reach our goal?

1495
02:10:40,920 --> 02:10:43,230
Vuslat (The ultimate union)
is one home.

1496
02:10:43,710 --> 02:10:46,200
Home is the whole world.

1497
02:10:47,000 --> 02:10:48,160
Eyvallah.

1498
02:10:48,940 --> 02:10:51,900
So what stops us is not fear of death.

1499
02:10:51,900 --> 02:10:53,120
No.

1500
02:10:54,570 --> 02:10:56,990
We will erase them.

1501
02:11:01,660 --> 02:11:03,220
Can I come in, my Bey?

1502
02:11:04,670 --> 02:11:05,740
Come!

1503
02:11:11,170 --> 02:11:12,320
My Bey!

1504
02:11:12,720 --> 02:11:13,680
It's Aktemur.

1505
02:11:14,600 --> 02:11:15,700
He is seriously injured.

1506
02:11:19,110 --> 02:11:20,070
What?

1507
02:11:40,060 --> 02:11:41,750
Protect him, my Allah.

1508
02:11:42,440 --> 02:11:44,480
Let him see his mother again.

1509
02:11:55,090 --> 02:11:56,310
I didn't do it.

1510
02:11:58,980 --> 02:12:00,210
I wouldn't.

1511
02:12:13,900 --> 02:12:15,670
No, Bengi sister, no.

1512
02:12:16,270 --> 02:12:18,460
They chose Oktem Bey
as a sacrifice.

1513
02:12:18,820 --> 02:12:22,060
Otherwise, all these misfortunes
cannot happen at the same time.

1514
02:12:22,190 --> 02:12:23,300
I'm sure of that!

1515
02:12:23,700 --> 02:12:26,830
Our reputation reaches the
seven seas, Bayindir Bey.

1516
02:12:27,070 --> 02:12:30,200
The ones who want to sacrifice us
will be punished dearly.

1517
02:12:31,880 --> 02:12:33,380
We'll go through this.

1518
02:12:33,790 --> 02:12:35,640
These days will surely pass.

1519
02:12:35,640 --> 02:12:36,790
Of course we will.

1520
02:12:37,330 --> 02:12:39,240
Every cloud has a silver lining.

1521
02:12:39,300 --> 02:12:40,920
Can I come in, Bengi Hatun?

1522
02:12:41,060 --> 02:12:42,430
Come!

1523
02:12:46,850 --> 02:12:50,350
Alcicek Hatun tried to kill
Gunduz Bey's son Aktemur.

1524
02:12:50,580 --> 02:12:51,810
What are you saying?

1525
02:12:52,950 --> 02:12:54,160
What are you saying?

1526
02:12:54,770 --> 02:12:55,930
Alcicek!

1527
02:12:56,850 --> 02:12:58,310
I told her not to...

1528
02:12:58,650 --> 02:13:01,330
I told her not to act crazy!

1529
02:13:02,180 --> 02:13:04,100
Is Aktemur Bey alive?
What is the situation?

1530
02:13:04,440 --> 02:13:05,530
I do not know.

1531
02:13:05,770 --> 02:13:07,320
They took her to prison.

1532
02:13:08,650 --> 02:13:11,020
I will burn Yenisehir!

1533
02:13:12,810 --> 02:13:14,080
It is enough!

1534
02:13:14,210 --> 02:13:16,250
What they have taken from me is enough!

1535
02:13:16,830 --> 02:13:18,410
Alps!

1536
02:13:24,730 --> 02:13:28,430
We'll crush everyone.

1537
02:13:29,720 --> 02:13:30,800
Get ready.

1538
02:13:36,400 --> 02:13:37,500
O Healer!

1539
02:13:45,360 --> 02:13:46,740
Who did this?

1540
02:13:47,750 --> 02:13:49,340
Tell me!

1541
02:13:52,340 --> 02:13:55,660
Hatuns, tell me who did this!

1542
02:13:59,830 --> 02:14:00,920
Son.

1543
02:14:01,220 --> 02:14:03,270
He is entrusted to me by my brother.

1544
02:14:05,720 --> 02:14:08,220
My Bey, it's Oktem Bey's daughter.

1545
02:14:08,440 --> 02:14:09,970
Alcicek did this.

1546
02:14:15,440 --> 02:14:18,090
That girl, that girl!

1547
02:14:18,190 --> 02:14:20,330
She did it in a treacherous way!

1548
02:14:21,400 --> 02:14:23,860
She set the trap!

1549
02:14:23,860 --> 02:14:26,290
How could she do this to my son?!

1550
02:14:48,020 --> 02:14:49,410
Alcicek.

1551
02:14:53,180 --> 02:14:54,420
Alcicek.

1552
02:15:19,710 --> 02:15:20,930
Aktemur.

1553
02:15:21,270 --> 02:15:22,660
Aktemur.

1554
02:15:32,140 --> 02:15:33,280
Aktemur.

1555
02:15:33,700 --> 02:15:35,800
Open your eyes!
Open your eyes!

1556
02:15:36,190 --> 02:15:37,070
Aktemur!

1557
02:15:37,240 --> 02:15:38,150
Aktemur!

1558
02:15:38,150 --> 02:15:39,820
Calm down, Ayse.

1559
02:15:39,980 --> 02:15:41,130
Aktemur!

1560
02:15:41,600 --> 02:15:42,620
Aktemur!

1561
02:15:43,050 --> 02:15:44,170
Aktemur!

1562
02:15:44,480 --> 02:15:45,680
Open your eyes!

1563
02:15:45,680 --> 02:15:46,810
Aktemur!

1564
02:15:48,070 --> 02:15:50,810
We will erase the devil.

1565
02:15:54,660 --> 02:15:57,840
They know how judicious we are,
and they use this.

1566
02:15:58,260 --> 02:16:03,260
I swear we'll hang them on the gallows!

1567
02:16:05,690 --> 02:16:06,910
Aktemur!

1568
02:16:10,570 --> 02:16:11,760
My Allah!

1569
02:16:12,120 --> 02:16:14,830
Aktemur!
Aktemur!

1570
02:16:14,980 --> 02:16:16,380
Aktemur!

1571
